{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20","id":1147923,"title":"Modern RPG Safety and Wraith20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-07T21:43:59-07:00","id":1147923,"title":"Modern RPG Safety and Wraith20","content":"The hobby has come a long, long way since Wraith was originally published, and in many ways the current storygame renaissance seems more welcome to a moody, collaborative game about ghosts and their baggage than the Wild West of the 90s. One of the things we\u2019ve thankfully come a long way on is explicitly providing tools to keep players safe: session zeroes, discussion of lines and veils, the X card... Wraith perhaps suffered because it is a game strongly about personal suffering, with ready parallels to mental health, addiction, abuse, and suicide in the fiction (or sometimes, not metaphors at all), and with the potential for intens emotional bleed, it may have been too unruly for the hobby of the time.<br /> <br /> So I have to ask: will Wraith20 incorporate some of these newer tools into it? I can\u2019t imagine play without them, and in thinking about how much Wraith seems to share with younger offerings like Monsterhearts or Bluebeard\u2019s Bride, I can\u2019t help but hope for it to learn modern games\u2019 best lessons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T12:24:22-07:00","id":1148087,"title":"","content":"It might also be worth mentioning that The Shoah book was one of the most mature takes on the holocaust in a fiction book in my opinion<br /> <br /> As if wether they well incorporate these safety tools, doubt it, nWoD writers have some sensitivity when it comes to their players, 20th anniversary and contemporary oWoD writers are trying to be painfully edgy and completely misunderstood what &quot;mature themes&quot; really suggest","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","user":"Shawarbaaz","date":". 10-08-2017, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T13:55:20-07:00","id":1148113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1148087#post1148087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might also be worth mentioning that The Shoah book was one of the most mature takes on the holocaust in a fiction book in my opinion<br /> <br /> As if wether they well incorporate these safety tools, doubt it, nWoD writers have some sensitivity when it comes to their players, 20th anniversary and contemporary oWoD writers are trying to be painfully edgy and completely misunderstood what &quot;mature themes&quot; really suggest</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way have the 20th anniversary edition writers been &quot;painfully edgy&quot;? They've been curating all of the old stuff and re-tuning it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T14:26:00-07:00","id":1148118,"title":"","content":"Always found CWoD to be Painfully campy to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T14:30:35-07:00","id":1148121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1148087#post1148087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">20th anniversary and contemporary oWoD writers are trying to be painfully edgy and completely misunderstood what &amp;quot;mature themes&amp;quot; really suggest</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a hard time believing things are as bad as people getting nuWW and OPP mixed up or believing they are exactly the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T01:42:20-07:00","id":1148243,"title":"","content":"Other than Brucato making some cringingly eye-rolly (but well meaning) decisions and letting magical thinking seep into places it doesn't belong - the immediate thing that springs to mind is his approach to trans people in M20, which suffers from letting magical thoughts on gender binaries and mystic polarities seep into a place it doesn't belong - the 20th anniversary editions are about as far from 'painfully edgy' as any pre-NWW oWoD content has ever been, from what I've seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T13:34:44-07:00","id":1148414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1148243#post1148243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than Brucato making some cringingly eye-rolly (but well meaning) decisions and letting magical thinking seep into places it doesn't belong - the immediate thing that springs to mind is his approach to trans people in M20, which suffers from letting magical thoughts on gender binaries and mystic polarities seep into a place it doesn't belong - the 20th anniversary editions are about as far from 'painfully edgy' as any pre-NWW oWoD content has ever been, from what I've seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait what?<br /> <br /> Like, I'm aware of the criticisms of Brucato injecting too much of his personal beliefs into M20 (going through Book of Secrets right now and...yeah I can see this kind of thing taking people out of reading the book), but what's wrong with his writings on trans peoples?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T13:44:22-07:00","id":1148421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1148414#post1148414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait what?<br /> <br /> Like, I'm aware of the criticisms of Brucato injecting too much of his personal beliefs into M20 (going through Book of Secrets right now and...yeah I can see this kind of thing taking people out of reading the book), but what's wrong with his writings on trans peoples?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak to M20, but I know there's a pretty nasty tendency to take trans characters and extrapolate their identities into some kind of transgressive magical form, arguing that their gender is inherently liminal and magical because it's outside the norm.<br /> <br /> Also, I know older Ascension material has been... less than great about trans folks. Not so fond memories of the Chinese infernalists who live as women.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T14:05:03-07:00","id":1148432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1148421#post1148421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't speak to M20, but I know there's a pretty nasty tendency to take trans characters and extrapolate their identities into some kind of transgressive magical form, arguing that their gender is inherently liminal and magical because it's outside the norm.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I know trans people and third gender people who do explore that in their spirituality, so it doesn\u2019t bother me that that is included (just as their are some cis Mages who explore cultural gender associations and symbols in their paradigms) - but certainly trans mages whose paradigm has nothing at all to do with their gender should ALSO have prominent representation so that isn\u2019t inherently seen as representative while its existent.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the Wu-Keng needed to go!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-09-2017, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T14:57:28-07:00","id":1148449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1148121#post1148121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a hard time believing things are as bad as people getting nuWW and OPP mixed up or believing they are exactly the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, NuWW certainly fits the bill so far. The OPP writers for 20th products most certainly do not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T15:42:04-07:00","id":1148453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1148243#post1148243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than Brucato making some cringingly eye-rolly (but well meaning) decisions and letting magical thinking seep into places it doesn't belong - the immediate thing that springs to mind is his approach to trans people in M20, which suffers from letting magical thoughts on gender binaries and mystic polarities seep into a place it doesn't belong - the 20th anniversary editions are about as far from 'painfully edgy' as any pre-NWW oWoD content has ever been, from what I've seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>C20 did not share this issue, so I'm assuming that M20 is the odd one out and that Wr20 will be more in line with the other three (particularly because it shares a &quot;making up for not having a Revised edition&quot; thing in common with C20).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T16:06:16-07:00","id":1148462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1148453#post1148453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> C20 did not share this issue, so I'm assuming that M20 is the odd one out and that Wr20 will be more in line with the other three (particularly because it shares a &quot;making up for not having a Revised edition&quot; thing in common with C20).</div> </div> </div> </div>The most you could argue for C20 is its depiction of the antagonist group Shadow Court. <br /> <br /> With its association and apparent connection to movements like Occupy and BLM...but that\u2019s about it. And the book doesn\u2019t really dwell on it much and I\u2019d say it\u2019s less offensive and more just...odd. <br /> <br /> (And from my understanding, the Shadow Court has always been kind of weird in CtD)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T06:05:36-07:00","id":1148563,"title":"","content":"Whatever the flaws of other lines, Wraith is strongly connected to issues of depression, mental illness, and self destruction and presents unique challenges because of it. Even if these topics are approached with the best of care they are still going to be painful for some players. Indeed, when the connection between Shadowguiding and these issues isn't explicit, it often unnerves and upsets players without anyone understanding why. To that end, I would be very surprised if the Roleplaying chapter didn't have at least some advice for approaching these issues in game as well as a sidebar or two with tools like the X card. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T01:53:38-07:00","id":1148779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1148414#post1148414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait what?<br /> <br /> Like, I'm aware of the criticisms of Brucato injecting too much of his personal beliefs into M20 (going through Book of Secrets right now and...yeah I can see this kind of thing taking people out of reading the book), but what's wrong with his writings on trans peoples?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, he does two things. First, he treats trans people a few times as constituting a distinct third gender. While I am a pretty firm believer in third (and more, for that matter) genders and genderqueer/non-binary status, the vast majority of transpeople are not third gender but very much either male or female. The second is a couple of places where he suggests that the trans identity - occupying the 'third gender' space - is inherently mystical.<br /> <br /> Neither are especially bad, which is why I called them cringey but well-meaning. They're bad in the same way that going 'all &lt;ethnicity&gt; are magic because of &lt;ethnicity!&gt;' It's the sort of thing that used to be kind of inclusive, but is now fairly dated as an approach. The former is basically an error of phrasing and contextualization ('transpeople break the binary, therefore they are outside the binary and constitute a third gender' as opposed to 'some transpeople's identity lies entirely outside the binary, while the majority rest mostly inside it other than the social challenge they present to its most rigid implementations') rather than anything done in malice.<br /> <br /> The latter I find especially annoying as an occultist, since it obscures and dilutes the actual 'magical symbolism' of the hermaphrodite by confusing that lofty symbol with physically intersex and transgender people. The reason the hermaphrodite has a certain magical luster as a concept is to do with the sublimation and exaltation of the male/female binary into a single being, emblematically being also the sublimation of the larger positive/negative dark/light sacred/profane opposition into a unified whole, which is the aim of a fairly large swathe of (mostly dualistic) Western esoteric thought as a whole. It's nothing to do with 'and Jane has a penis, so she's magic'.<br /> <br /> To be clear, since it's come up before, there's nothing wrong with having trans characters who've had their experiences of transitioning provide a source of insight, strength, or mystical awakening (indeed, physical changes, social status changes, and exploration of boundaries make great sources for those things regardless of whether its gender or something else) - it's just a bit on the nose to declare the trans experience innately magical (outside of the definition of magic that defines it as the process of a person, by means of their will (not their Will), exerting a change on reality, in which case it is magical but no more so than anything else. LMdQ uses the example of asking for a glass of water from someone - by this loose definition, this is an act of magic) outside of that individualized context or certain very specific third-gender traditions in non-Western (or even Archaic Western) cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T03:44:18-07:00","id":1150593,"title":"","content":"Wraith never stuck me as a system where these guidelines have to be explicitly and bluntly spelled out. It's basically collaborative therapy, the game, so I always ran, or participated in, games with a zeroth session and hard/soft limits. <br /> <br /> It might be my background in BDSM. but it never occurred to me that this is not a self-evident thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T07:31:05-07:00","id":1150995,"title":"","content":"It has been a very long time since I've played any RPG, let alone Wraith. Since it is near and dear to my heart, I hope I can provide some kind of answer. This game can run the gamut from shallow to drowning ocean depths. I have ran groups where the focus was always on the Shadow tempting the player, and we had amateur psychology sessions as he dealt with his pain from a deceased parent. I've also ran games where it was D&amp;D but dead. It was about destroying Spectres, amasssing power, and kicking Oblivion in the groin. I love the world for my own reasons, but its such a great take on the afterlife I will adapt the setting to my players. It took me the longest time to realize, there is no right way to run the game. Fun, therapy, sorrow. Any story you write with Wraith starts with death, and we all handle it differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T14:41:56-07:00","id":1152299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20#post1147923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One of the things we\u2019ve thankfully come a long way on is explicitly providing tools to keep players safe: session zeroes, discussion of lines and veils, the X card... Wraith perhaps suffered because it is a game strongly about personal suffering, with ready parallels to mental health, addiction, abuse, and suicide in the fiction (or sometimes, not metaphors at all), and with the potential for intens emotional bleed, it may have been too unruly for the hobby of the time.<br /> <br /> So I have to ask: will Wraith20 incorporate some of these newer tools into it? I can\u2019t imagine play without them, and in thinking about how much Wraith seems to share with younger offerings like Monsterhearts or Bluebeard\u2019s Bride, I can\u2019t help but hope for it to learn modern games\u2019 best lessons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never had anything like that and neither me or my friends had issues with our sessions, not once. We know each others and we can take whatever the other says, especially if we meet them only in a game. Personally I've a quirk to have my friends cats die horribly as their Werewolf character eats them while hunting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, I may sound a bit old style, but I think people should grow up a bit to play Wraith.<br /> It's maybe the most mature game of all the WW setting and you just shouldn't play it if you're too sensitive to need X cards.<br /> I see a lot of people today fearing confrontations so much that they hide behind a safe space the moment they touch something it doesn't compute for their mind and I'm really scared at the thought of seeing third wave feminism behaviours in RPGs. I may be wrong but I think I even saw somewhere the suggestion to have the Shadows provoke the characters on their players' weak points, just to augment immersion.<br /> <br /> Back in the '90s, when people protested against the role playing games because of their high content of paganism, violence and Christian heresies in their games the WW wrote some polite &quot;fuck you&quot; in their manuals, clarifying how it was only a game and that they didn't endorse any kind of behaviour or philosophy in their games. I wonder how they games would have been if they've instead put &quot;nope&quot; cards inside just to have Mormons play.<br /> <br /> The whole point of RPing is that you're not your character and you should not project yourself in it, if you can't separate character and player then you should probably start with something easier and not Wraith: just like you said, it's a game about facing pain and oriented to people willing to feel strong emotions in their sessions. If you don't like it you should probably play something else rather than throwing yourself in a game that forces you to face death and loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T15:18:20-07:00","id":1152310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1152299#post1152299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, I may sound a bit old style, but I think people should grow up a bit to play Wraith.<br /> It's maybe the most mature game of all the WW setting and you just shouldn't play it if you're too sensitive to need X cards.<br /> I see a lot of people today fearing confrontations so much that they hide behind a safe space the moment they touch something it doesn't compute for their mind and I'm really scared at the thought of seeing third wave feminism behaviours in RPGs. I may be wrong but I think I even saw somewhere the suggestion to have the Shadows provoke the characters on their players' weak points, just to augment immersion.<br /> <br /> The whole point of RPing is that you're not your character and you should not project yourself in it, if you can't separate character and player then you should probably start with something easier and not Wraith: just like you said, it's a game about facing pain and oriented to people willing to feel strong emotions in their sessions. If you don't like it you should probably play something else rather than throwing yourself in a game that forces you to face death and loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's pretty offensive to act like people who want to deal with sensitive themes with some form of safety valve need to &quot;grow up,&quot; and I think your random call out of feminism as some kind of blight on the hobby is pretty much uncalled for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 10-23-2017, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T18:23:10-07:00","id":1152348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1152310#post1152310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's pretty offensive to act like people who want to deal with sensitive themes with some form of safety valve need to &quot;grow up,&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's pretty offensive to think that people should be treated like porcelain dolls.<br /> <br /> This kind of obsession to shelter adult people's psyches is exactly what concerns me. I assume that grown-ups have the maturity to protect themselves quite enough and that can pick their own games, just like they pick their favourite movies: if they don't like scare jumps or ghastly settings they won't watch horror movies, and even if they do it &quot;just to try&quot; they can stand up and go away at any time.<br /> And there's a specific subgroup of third wave feminists quite notorious both for overreacting and bullying people that think differently; so, even if I don't want to call out the whole feminism I think it's not really that random to write that I'm troubled when someone calls for safeguards on a role playing game. I mean no offense to you or any good hearted feminist out there, but it really feels excessive to me.<br /> <br /> Because, just like 20 years ago when Wraith was first published, this is just a game and your character is not you. If you can't take a ghost story is fine, we don't have all the same tastes and as a group we're theng going to play something else, but what I'm definitely not having is people agreeing to the ghost story but raising a hand and say that the master should stop describing his troubling scene. Because I want that description and I think I deserve a certain kind of emotional trip in a game tailored precisely for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 10-23-2017, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T18:43:04-07:00","id":1152353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1152348#post1152348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's pretty offensive to think that people should be treated like porcelain dolls.<br /> <br /> This kind of obsession to shelter adult people's psyches is exactly what concerns me. I assume that grown-ups have the maturity to protect themselves quite enough and that can pick their own games, just like they pick their favourite movies: if they don't like scare jumps or ghastly settings they won't watch horror movies, and even if they do it &quot;just to try&quot; they can stand up and go away at any time.<br /> And there's a specific subgroup of third wave feminists quite notorious both for overreacting and bullying people that think differently; so, even if I don't want to call out the whole feminism I think it's not really that random to write that I'm troubled when someone calls for safeguards on a role playing game. I mean no offense to you or any good hearted feminist out there, but it really feels excessive to me.<br /> <br /> Because, just like 20 years ago when Wraith was first published, this is just a game and your character is not you. If you can't take a ghost story is fine, we don't have all the same tastes and as a group we're theng going to play something else, but what I'm definitely not having is people agreeing to the ghost story but raising a hand and say that the master should stop describing his troubling scene. Because I want that description and I think I deserve a certain kind of emotional trip in a game tailored precisely for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your rambling about feminism as some kind of insidious evil ruining the hobby is pretty Not Great.<br /> <br /> I don't understand acting like offering some optional mechanical guard rails and advice in a book is some great offense to you. If you don't want to use them, you're more than welcome to, but going beyond <i>I don't like this! </i>and spiraling off into a huge slam on people who like to feel more comfortable or safe during a <i>hobby designed for play</i> as somehow being fragile or immature is needlessly cruel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T00:57:30-07:00","id":1152427,"title":"","content":"There is a difference between recognizing the potential for psychological distress that certain themes can create for people with past situations dealing with them and taking the appropriate steps to ensure that a game that deals with those themes - a recreational past time, usually not a professional therapy session - has tools and mechanisms in place. Those tools and mechanisms won't be needed for every group, and their existence does not mean you need to use them or that they will be used at the drop of a hat. When a game very specifically and primarily deals with confronting traumas, past experiences, and abuse then it is doubly important that there be an awareness that for some people, maybe one of those themes will need some special handling - or maybe it won't, but it can't hurt to have the tools right there.<br /> <br /> This is not about third wave feminism or treating people like porcelain dolls. This is just being a responsible adult capable of empathy and of understanding post-traumatic stress and anxiety. This is because the safeguards being considered are not about, as you have nominated, 'scare jumps' or 'ghastly settings', but rather things like sexual assault, suicide, extreme mental illness, self-harm, and substance abuse. There is also no suggestion that these topics should be off limits, as you tried to insinuate with your earlier commentary on 90s WW's 'fuck off!' disclaimers, which were written at a time where that very much <i>was</i> the suggestion. The only suggestion, the only request, is that since the game can get real dark real fast in ways touching on actual traumatic experiences for actual people, it should have tools in place to facilitate keeping it enjoyable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T01:28:56-07:00","id":1152432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1152427#post1152427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a difference between recognizing the potential for psychological distress that certain themes can create for people with past situations dealing with them and taking the appropriate steps to ensure that a game that deals with those themes - a recreational past time, usually not a professional therapy session - has tools and mechanisms in place. Those tools and mechanisms won't be needed for every group, and their existence does not mean you need to use them or that they will be used at the drop of a hat. When a game very specifically and primarily deals with confronting traumas, past experiences, and abuse then it is doubly important that there be an awareness that for some people, maybe one of those themes will need some special handling - or maybe it won't, but it can't hurt to have the tools right there.<br /> <br /> This is not about third wave feminism or treating people like porcelain dolls. This is just being a responsible adult capable of empathy and of understanding post-traumatic stress and anxiety. This is because the safeguards being considered are not about, as you have nominated, 'scare jumps' or 'ghastly settings', but rather things like sexual assault, suicide, extreme mental illness, self-harm, and substance abuse. There is also no suggestion that these topics should be off limits, as you tried to insinuate with your earlier commentary on 90s WW's 'fuck off!' disclaimers, which were written at a time where that very much <i>was</i> the suggestion. The only suggestion, the only request, is that since the game can get real dark real fast in ways touching on actual traumatic experiences for actual people, it should have tools in place to facilitate keeping it enjoyable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Said more eloquently than I could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T04:22:56-07:00","id":1152459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1152427#post1152427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only suggestion, the only request, is that since the game can get real dark real fast in ways touching on actual traumatic experiences for actual people, it should have tools in place to facilitate keeping it enjoyable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it so wrong to expect that an adult has enough self-knowledge to refuse a game that deals with death and traumas if they have history? Or, is it wrong to expect that in a group of friends the ST knows who the others are and suggests a different campaign, knowing that one of the players had to deal with his brother's suicide?<br /> <br /> The point is that I want to deal with suicides in my Wraith game - hell, maybe I even think suicide is a cool way for my character to die. But rather than having someone asking me to to redo the background because one of us can't deal with suicides I'd rather play something else (if i'm with friends) or play without him (if we're strangers); because, as a player, this is exactly the kind of dark theme I want to explore in a game made esplicitly to deal with pain and I think I have the right to ask for them.<br /> <br /> I'm not against a session zero (even if calling it this way is needlessly formal), but rather than talking about safeguards only I'd like to talk about the creative agenda and what we're expecting from the game, so that all the players can be on the same page about the chronicle. So, if someone is uncomfortable with the themes the ST or the other players are bringing out he can say it right there and leave the group the chance to decide how to proceed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T04:45:27-07:00","id":1152463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1152459#post1152459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it so wrong to expect that an adult has enough self-knowledge to refuse a game that deals with death and traumas if they have history?</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is saying that. We are, however, suggesting that the door should not be slammed shut in people's faces and there is in fact a middle ground between 'in' and 'out'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or, is it wrong to expect that in a group of friends the ST knows who the others are and suggests a different campaign, knowing that one of the players had to deal with his brother's suicide? </div> </div> </div>Again, no one is saying that. The reason why tools like a red card are useful is because traumas are often unknown to other people (often even very intimate friends, even long-term romanticpartners) because they can be exceptionally personal and, quite frankly, not the business of everyone present at the table. This is especially the case where you have new groups or groups trying a new genre involving these themes where previously they played only, say, Pugmire and it was unlikely to be an issue. It is also entirely possible that a sexual assault survivor (purely as an example) may be comfortable playing in a game where that is a theme and where the ST is aware of their history, but unaware of certain details that push it into not-okay territory (a particular form of assault, say).<br /> <br /> A responsive ST is the ideal. These tools do nothing more than give them more to work with and - using the card again - players a way to quietly signal, without having to explain to a table of people, that something is either edging into or is in outright discomforting territory for them. The response could be a temporary pause, a check in, a readjustment - or whatever else the player(s) and ST feel is appropriate.<br /> <br /> Because triggers are rarely as straightforward as people think and can be complex and highly situational, discussion beforehand in 'session zero' or the use of cards is an excellent way to ensure there are no <i>accidental</i> steps into that territory. It's one thing entirely to explore suicide or child abuse with a player who knows it's coming and has some baggage around it (in those circumstances it may even be helpful to them, if handled appropriately, by giving them a safe place in which to recontextualize things and process emotion) and quite another to spring it on people unsuspecting where it's a risk factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point is that I want to deal with suicides in my Wraith game - hell, maybe I even think suicide is a cool way for my character to die. </div> </div> </div>Cool. No one is saying you can't - just that it's generally good practice, as a mature adult, to be aware that certain subject matter may be difficult for others and to have empathy. It's the same reason Aussie tv shows mention a warning on content with indigenous persons who have died that this is the case - there are cultural taboos that mean that for some indigenous viewers, that content is deeply upsetting/ritually impure/absolutely forbidden, and it's just plain old polite and decent to let those people know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But rather than having someone asking me to to redo the background because one of us can't deal with suicides I'd rather play something else (if i'm with friends) or play without him (if we're strangers); </div> </div> </div>No one is saying you can't get up and leave the group or suggest a different game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> because, as a player, this is exactly the kind of dark theme I want to explore in a game made esplicitly to deal with pain and I think I have the right to ask for them. </div> </div> </div>And the other players have the exact same right to ask that certain themes be put off limits or handled in a careful way - especially if the pain they're dealing with is one <i>you have no experience with</i>. Your enjoyment of a game should not come before the emotional wellbeing of another human being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not against a session zero (even if calling it this way is needlessly formal), but rather than talking about safeguards only I'd like to talk about the creative agenda and what we're expecting from the game, so that all the players can be on the same page about the chronicle. So, if someone is uncomfortable with the themes the ST or the other players are bringing out he can say it right there and leave the group the chance to decide how to proceed. </div> </div> </div>No one is suggesting that this not be the case. Session zero - I'm with you on disliking the terminology, incidentally - encompasses creative agenda, expectations, character generation, all of that as well as an opportunity to flag certain subjects as needing delicate handling or being too sensitive. All that is being sought are additional tools to make it easier for often socially awkward people to have the discussion about how to proceed in a mature and safe way, and to prevent it from going pearshaped when it has.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T18:11:24-07:00","id":1152657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1152463#post1152463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is especially the case where you have new groups or groups trying a new genre involving these themes where previously they played only, say, Pugmire and it was unlikely to be an issue. It is also entirely possible that a sexual assault survivor (purely as an example) may be comfortable playing in a game where that is a theme and where the ST is aware of their history, but unaware of certain details that push it into not-okay territory (a particular form of assault, say).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, you can get trigger-issues from ANYWHERE. You want to play Pugmire, cool... I had my ear bitten off by a dog when I was 8. They reattached it. No one can tell. There definitely exists the possibility that snarly-ear-ripping-dog-violence could be problematic for me. (Not that I have any issues about it. I was more upset by the fact they put down the dog after than I was by the hospital trip....I genuinely have more issues from some car-wrecks I've been in, but the possibility exists).<br /> <br /> I doubt if ANYONE from my gaming group knows that and I've known everyone in the group for at least 7 years and a couple from up to 25 years in which we've played together. Why would they? I don't talk about it. I don't think about it. BUT, all that aside, I could easily agree to play Pugmire and, if it was more of a concern for me, a great ST might be able to &quot;trigger&quot; something, I guess... probably not, but the possibility is there. <br /> <br /> And that's a nothing. That's not a suicide attempt. That's not an unexpected pregnancy at a bad time. That's not an addiction issue. That's not a major illness and the resulting consequences. That's not coping with issues relating to cognition on a daily basis. Any or all of those things could be in play with people you THINK you know because you've been gaming with them. I bet the cat thing wouldn't be a joke AT ALL to someone who saw their pet torn to pieces in front of them or found the remnants of their cat after it was mangled. Going over what's going down in a game that is specifically going to be mucking around in the deepest parts of people's psyches explicitly? Not a bad thing. <br /> <br /> This is a game where suicide is effectively a career path.... Being beat to death in a back alley for some aspect of your person (race, gender, whatever) is actually a door to future advancement. Where body horror issues go off the rails with things like Moliate. Where taboo subjects like slavery are put back on the table front and center alongside Dachau lamp shades so de jure they're the coin of the realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T19:03:49-07:00","id":1152670,"title":"","content":"Okay, my take on the subject: I don't mind it. I didn't mind the sidebars about transgenderism and mysticism and pronouns in M20, neither the sidebar in the D&amp;D 5e PHB, neither the few lines about using hard topics in W20, or the same stuff in Paizo's Horror Adventures.<br /> <br /> I don't need X-cards and the other &quot;modern safety mechanisms&quot;. I think they aren't even really good solutions to the problem, since if you have to tap it, you've been already encountered the traumatic scene (although it could put a short end to it, but that has other negative sides, regarding the game and story itself). So, I don't need it and don't particularly like it, but Wraith is a dark game (honestly, I find the setting interesting as a background and Wraiths are interesting NPCs to me, but I'm not particularly inclined to play it as a PC, it's too much nihilism for me and I <i>love </i>Vampire), but other people clearly want it to be there, so hey, what's a sidebar, or a column of text? As long as it doesn't take away from the game, from its darkness (pun not intended), as long as WoD games are still dealing openly with hard topics, and don't shy away from them (which is a much bigger issue, in general, nowadays as weel as catering t certain narrative here and there), I really don't care if there's some text about safety mechanisms in the ST chapter.<br /> <br /> Sneering at the &quot;edgyness&quot; of WoD is far more toxic, IMO and actually bad for the game and setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 10-24-2017, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T17:35:24-07:00","id":1152984,"title":"","content":"Wraith is a game designed to make you feel uncomfortable so it's a little weird to hear people talk about avoiding that discomfort while they're playing it. <br /> <br /> Of course, there is a narrow possibility that a player who happily signed on for a game about death at literally every moment and with another player specifically roleplaying the darkest part of their character's mind could encounter some other subject during the game that makes them way more uncomfortable than those things, and in that case X cards would be helpful. I don't think Wraith is any more subject to that risk than any other game; it has plenty of darkness, but it's pretty obvious, and X cards are for unanticipated triggers. <br /> <br /> I would be annoyed if someone used an X card during an entirely basic description of Deathsight. I wouldn't ask for an explanation of course, but I'd wonder why they agreed to play Wraith in the first place if such a basic component of it discomforts them enough to stop the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T18:06:33-07:00","id":1152994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1152984#post1152984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be annoyed if someone used an X card during an entirely basic description of Deathsight. I wouldn't ask for an explanation of course, but I'd wonder why they agreed to play Wraith in the first place if such a basic component of it discomforts them enough to stop the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I frequently feel some people just want to play WoD, but not with all the implications, due to personal reasons. Mind those reasons aren't invalid, but when they're going straight against the core premises of the specific game, or established setting elements, I just have a hard time to understand why those people insist on playing those games? Ok, probably because they like other elements, or the <i>idea</i> they have about the game, but not the actual execution.<br /> <br /> Still, if you don't like to see deep, ingrained and even somewhat unchangeable inequality in society, Masquerade isn't the best game for you. Same with Werewolf and bigotry. If death or other, deeply traumatic things could bring up your own traumas to the point that it's harmful to your well-being and gaming experience, Wraith isn't the best game for you. If you're just bothered by the implications of a setting described as &quot;our world, but even more shitty&quot;, then, probably WoD in general isn't really the best for you.<br /> <br /> Thing is, I and a lot of other people have fell in love with WoD, because it is what it is. Don't like it? There are million games out there with similar, but differently executed themes. WoD should remain &quot;edgy&quot;, thanks.<br /> <br /> To reiterate: I really don't mind some description of safety mechanics in the book, as long as they aren't taking up much space. There are other, targeted publications for that. In a WoD book, I want WoD material and WoD specific ST advice, but a sidebar, or a column? Well, yes, why not?<br /> <br /> Also, despite some people's tendency to throw as much mud on WW as possible, I'm actually fully expecting to see some talk about safety mechanisms in V5, considering the developer team and how important the whole concept is in Nordic LARP and how central and prominent it was in their big LARPs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 10-25-2017, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T19:26:56-07:00","id":1153010,"title":"","content":"Surprisingly, I am an enormous fan of the 'edgy' WoD, as you'd put it. This isn't an attempt to cut that down - it's an attempt to provide tools to make it easier to explore with a broader audience. Also, why on earth are we now debating the use of an X card during a basic description of death sight? It has zero relationship to what those of us advocating for the use of the tools are talking about, just like the random rant upthread about feminism didn't.<br /> <br /> Just to reiterate: Suggesting these tools be in place is not an attempt to 'cut down' on the 'edge'. It is not a suggestion that they be used around basic gameplay mechanics (in a case where a person is so seriously affected by them that the use of X cards and safe words when describing a basic game mechanic or lore point, then yes, the game is probably not a good fit, and I don't think Lex or I would say otherwise) or an attempt to in some way neuter the game. It is not a suggestion that people shouldn't exercise common sense and good judgment when deciding if the game is appropriate for them - it's a suggestion that there be tools in place in case things take an unexpected turn, or a person is less able to handle it than they expected. No one on the side of these tools is going 'well, the basic themes of the game are bad/i don't like the implications of a shittier world/inequality upsets me, so x card please' - we're talking about a specific game in the line that deals with a lot more potential triggers than any other, and our comments are solely in reference to that basic aspect.<br /> <br /> We are very specifically addressing a game line where discussions of domestic violence, sexual abuse, suicide, and other serious and real problems is par for the course. The reason we're suggesting the tools might be good is because we are actually <i>fans</i> of the idea. You'll notice we aren't asking for it to change, we aren't asking 'please make suicide discussion off limits in the corebook thanks', we're asking 'hey, so, this game can get really dark, could it be a good idea to include a few basic and possibly helpful tools that have developed around games that deal with dark content?'<br /> <br /> Rambling complaints about feminism or intellectually dishonest attempts to paint the tools as being aimed at basic gameplay or attempts at defending the setting's 'edge' where no one is trying to blunt it - unless you define the setting's edge as 'has the potential to trigger unsuspecting players with severe emotional trauma from prior life experiences', that is - is unhelpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T19:38:58-07:00","id":1153013,"title":"","content":"Asking for mechanics like the X card is explicitly in favor of having triggering content in the game, so that it can exist in play responsibly and safely for all involved. The alternative answer is \u201cI\u2019d rather not have that content at all,\u201d which isn\u2019t what anyone advocating for this are saying.<br /> <br /> Anyone who doubts my cred is more than welcome to kiss my Silent Lrgion tattoo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T19:53:27-07:00","id":1153016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153010#post1153010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are very specifically addressing a game line where discussions of domestic violence, sexual abuse, suicide, and other serious and real problems is par for the course. The reason we're suggesting the tools might be good is because we are actually <i>fans</i> of the idea. You'll notice we aren't asking for it to change, we aren't asking 'please make suicide discussion off limits in the corebook thanks', we're asking 'hey, so, this game can get really dark, could it be a good idea to include a few basic and possibly helpful tools that have developed around games that deal with dark content?'<br /> <br /> Rambling complaints about feminism or intellectually dishonest attempts to paint the tools as being aimed at basic gameplay or attempts at defending the setting's 'edge' where no one is trying to blunt it - unless you define the setting's edge as 'has the potential to trigger unsuspecting players with severe emotional trauma from prior life experiences', that is - is unhelpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, you're arguing with nobody, at least not with me. I said I don't mind its inclusion in the ST chapter. If anyone is absolutely sure they want to try the game, for whatever reasons and then they find out during play that it's too much, but want to stay, at least for the session... Well, if you absolutely want to use it, because without it you fear serious trauma, then use it! I'm dealing with anxiety and panic attacks for years, I could comprehend it's potential necessity. However, as I said , I don't need it and I don't like it, because I see it as disruptive and because it's a slippery slope, in a dark game, to saying without any former explanation &quot;please exclude this&quot; and yes, it could, on the long run, lead to the setting losing its edge. It's not the x-card specifically, it's the whole phenomenon, the whole thought process that &quot;we don't want traumatic things in the game&quot;, because, well, an awful lot of things could be traumatic and this thought process is quite the death of dark games, IMO. If you're triggered badly by content quite paramount in Wraith, then how'd you read the corebook itself, or the supplements? That's the slippery slope, because then we'd start to exclude <i>those</i> thigs from the books and then <i>those other things</i> too and we'd end up with a sanitized WoD, after a time. Yes, no one of you advocated that specifically, I'm aware, but again, it's not the x-card specifically, or its responsible usage, when needed, it's where it could lead, over time.<br /> <br /> But again, if it's absolutely needed for a person, then use it! If we're conscious to avoid the castrating of the setting, then it's a tool and sometimes needed, as the least of evils in a hard situation. And also again, I don't mind it in the book, as sidebar, a half-page, or a full page at best, but I don't want pages upon pages of talk about safety mechanics in a WoD corebook. Write down the most necessary basics, then point the reader to appropriate publications and I'm okay with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 10-25-2017, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T20:02:58-07:00","id":1153018,"title":"","content":"My point is simply that X cards are meant to handle unexpectedly triggering content, and while Wraith has a lot of potentially triggering content, it's by no means unexpected. It wears its darkness on its sleeve. The OP suggested that Wraith uniquely needed notes about these mechanisms due to its dark content, and I disagree - it has no more unexpected dark content than any other WW game. <br /> <br /> I suppose someone being less able to handle the nature of Wraith than they thought makes sense, but even then, an X card isn't appropriate, because those topics aren't going to go away. If they realize they can't handle the topic of suicide, does the player whose character died of suicide now have to change his character? Are we suddenly going to magically assume no other wraiths became so via suicide? When the concept is a basic part of the game, you can't just move into the next scene, because the next scene will contain more of the same, and the one after that. The person would need to leave the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T20:20:12-07:00","id":1153022,"title":"","content":"I gotta say alot of what i'm seeing here is making me interested in wraith. Is it the next 'something20' to come out? And if not would it be worth it to get the last corebook? (apologies if this isnt the right thread to ask this)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T20:22:04-07:00","id":1153023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153018#post1153018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is simply that X cards are meant to handle unexpectedly triggering content, and while Wraith has a lot of potentially triggering content, it's by no means unexpected. It wears its darkness on its sleeve. The OP suggested that Wraith uniquely needed notes about these mechanisms due to its dark content, and I disagree - it has no more unexpected dark content than any other WW game.<br /> <br /> I suppose someone being less able to handle the nature of Wraith than they thought makes sense, but even then, an X card isn't appropriate, because those topics aren't going to go away. If they realize they can't handle the topic of suicide, does the player whose character died of suicide now have to change his character? Are we suddenly going to magically assume no other wraiths became so via suicide? When the concept is a basic part of the game, you can't just move into the next scene, because the next scene will contain more of the same, and the one after that. The person would need to leave the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit like playing vampire, when somebody can't handle the prospect of blood, potentially could have a serious breakdown by vivid descriptions of blood-drinking scenes, or find the potential parallels between feeding and rape deeply troubling. Ok, he could tap the x-card and the ST could fade to dark, or change the scene (I'd prefer the former, just to maintain story integrity), but the whole thing is just so ingrained into the game that after a while I'd ask &quot;why do you want to play this game?&quot;. For playing dark superheroes? Nothing's wrong with that, but there are better games for it and probably, for you. Especially if the majority of the party feels that the exclusion of profound thing takes away from the atmosphere of the game, even if they're happening, but always off the screen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T20:28:34-07:00","id":1153025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153016#post1153016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Look, you're arguing with nobody, at least not with me. I said I don't mind its inclusion in the ST chapter. If anyone is absolutely sure they want to try the game, for whatever reasons and then they find out during play that it's too much, but want to stay, at least for the session... Well, if you absolutely want to use it, because without it you fear serious trauma, then use it! I'm dealing with anxiety and panic attacks for years, I could comprehend it's potential necessity. However, as I said , I don't need it and I don't like it, because I see it as disruptive and because it's a slippery slope, in a dark game, to saying without any former explanation &quot;please exclude this&quot; and yes, it could, on the long run, lead to the setting losing its edge. It's not the x-card specifically, it's the whole phenomenon, the whole thought process that &quot;we don't want traumatic things in the game&quot;, because, well, an awful lot of things could be traumatic and this thought process is quite the death of dark games, IMO. If you're triggered badly by content quite paramount in Wraith, then how'd you read the corebook itself, or the supplements? That's the slippery slope, because then we'd start to exclude <i>those</i> thigs from the books and then <i>those other things</i> too and we'd end up with a sanitized WoD, after a time. Yes, no one of you advocated that specifically, I'm aware, but again, it's not the x-card specifically, or its responsible usage, when needed, it's where it could lead, over time.<br /> <br /> But again, if it's absolutely needed for a person, then use it! If we're conscious to avoid the castrating of the setting, then it's a tool and sometimes needed, as the least of evils in a hard situation. And also again, I don't mind it in the book, as sidebar, a half-page, or a full page at best, but I don't want pages upon pages of talk about safety mechanics in a WoD corebook. Write down the most necessary basics, then point the reader to appropriate publications and I'm okay with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See, you say I'm arguing with nobody, and then you type out a rant that shows exactly the same nonsense I was just arguing against. There is no slippery slope towards sanitization. The inclusion of safety tools is in fact more likely to shore up the slope and keep it from a landslide, just like planting trees on an actual hill. No one is trying to castrate the setting. No one is talking about pages upon pages of safety mechanics, though to be blunt Wraith would be one of the games where they would be most appropriate. The thought process is not, as you have identified, 'we don't want traumatic things in the game', it is 'traumatic content can trigger people in unexpected ways, and we would like to include that content. In order to avoid the accidental infliction of emotional distress on players in a way that is <i>not desired</i>, we should put in tools to address and minimize that risk factor.. The thought process is quite literally the opposite of what you are trying to identify it as.<br /> <br /> Further, you seem to be missing the level of fine detail involved. 'Suicide' as a whole is probably not triggering to people who will be okay playing Wraith. Suicide that winds up taking the same form as a past attempt by a player or that was the method used by a loved one might, and unlike 'dark themes' the exact method is not necessarily 'quite paramount'. Similarly, violent incidents are probably fine for most players, including those with a history of violence - but specifics, unintentionally included, can wind up sufficiently echoing an actual traumatic event that may or may not be resolved.<br /> <br /> Let's use me as a personal example. I can read the most horrific stories of child abuse all day every day without being genuinely triggered (I have, as a matter of fact, in the course of my studies for family law) - but if I read a relatively mild account that includes enough cross-matching points with the things that were done to my adopted sister, then I will lose all desire to continue and just want to lie down and cry or go kill something thanks to secondary-exposure PTSD responses. It is that kind of situation that these tools are designed to address, where something takes a turn from 'broadly exists' to 'very specifically hits a weak spot, either unexpectedly or with much more force than expected'. Is my trigger somehow 'quite paramount' to Wraith? No - child abuse may be, but the specific frame of reference isn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153018#post1153018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is simply that X cards are meant to handle unexpectedly triggering content, and while Wraith has a lot of potentially triggering content, it's by no means unexpected. It wears its darkness on its sleeve. The OP suggested that Wraith uniquely needed notes about these mechanisms due to its dark content, and I disagree - it has no more unexpected dark content than any other WW game.<br /> <br /> I suppose someone being less able to handle the nature of Wraith than they thought makes sense, but even then, an X card isn't appropriate, because those topics aren't going to go away. If they realize they can't handle the topic of suicide, does the player whose character died of suicide now have to change his character? Are we suddenly going to magically assume no other wraiths became so via suicide? When the concept is a basic part of the game, you can't just move into the next scene, because the next scene will contain more of the same, and the one after that. The person would need to leave the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>See my above post for more detail, but the premise here is not 'oh no, dark content'. It is the potential for the dark content to inadvertantly resemble actual traumatic experience. To use your suicide question, the pitch is not 'please ban suicide if a player finds it difficult' (quite frankly, I think most people on my side of the argument would agree that if someone is so severely affected that any discussion of suicide is a serious trigger, then Wraith is unlikely to be a solid fit for them until those issues are addressed), it is 'oh shit, it turns out John's dad killed himself in the exact same way as Tim's character and it's kind of fucking him up'. Suicide can remain in play, but the fine details can be adjusted to avoid it if the group thinks that's appropriate. Or, quite possibly, all that will be needed is for the game to take a beat, let John recover, and he might very well be fine going forward once it is no longer an unexpected shock.<br /> <br /> The expectation that an x card is a ban on material is wrong. It is a notice that 'this hit harder than expected, can we regroup for a second?' The group can then decide how to proceed. It is not 'I dislike &lt;x&gt;, ban it', it is 'as a mature adult, playing a game with other mature adults, I'm finding it difficult to have fun with &lt;x&gt; involved. Can we discuss this and figure out how to proceed?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T20:49:00-07:00","id":1153033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153025#post1153025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> See, you say I'm arguing with nobody, and then you type out a rant that shows exactly the same nonsense I was just arguing against. There is no slippery slope towards sanitization. The inclusion of safety tools is in fact more likely to shore up the slope and keep it from a landslide, just like planting trees on an actual hill. No one is trying to castrate the setting. No one is talking about pages upon pages of safety mechanics, though to be blunt Wraith would be one of the games where they would be most appropriate. The thought process is not, as you have identified, 'we don't want traumatic things in the game', it is 'traumatic content can trigger people in unexpected ways, and we would like to include that content. In order to avoid the accidental infliction of emotional distress on players in a way that is <i>not desired</i>, we should put in tools to address and minimize that risk factor.. The thought process is quite literally the opposite of what you are trying to identify it as.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, you say I was ranting without basis. I see the thing you say won't happen in books already, so we're clearly at a disagreement here and I'm okay with that, I'm still standing by my opinion and others could decide for themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Further, you seem to be missing the level of fine detail involved. 'Suicide' as a whole is probably not triggering to people who will be okay playing Wraith. Suicide that winds up taking the same form as a past attempt by a player or that was the method used by a loved one might, and unlike 'dark themes' the exact method is not necessarily 'quite paramount'. Similarly, violent incidents are probably fine for most players, including those with a history of violence - but specifics, unintentionally included, can wind up sufficiently echoing an actual traumatic event that may or may not be resolved.<br /> <br /> Let's use me as a personal example. I can read the most horrific stories of child abuse all day every day without being genuinely triggered (I have, as a matter of fact, in the course of my studies for family law) - but if I read a relatively mild account that includes enough cross-matching points with the things that were done to my adopted sister, then I will lose all desire to continue and just want to lie down and cry or go kill something thanks to secondary-exposure PTSD responses. It is that kind of situation that these tools are designed to address, where something takes a turn from 'broadly exists' to 'very specifically hits a weak spot, either unexpectedly or with much more force than expected'. Is my trigger somehow 'quite paramount' to Wraith? No - child abuse may be, but the specific frame of reference isn't. </div> </div> </div>And I'm clearly said that if absolutely necessary, then by all means, use it. I said, multiple times that's I think it's okay to include the basics about it in the book (but no, I'm not agreeing with doing it at length, again, there are targeted publications for that), but apparently you managed to somehow miss all that. From the standpoint of my own problems I could even see its potential usage as tool for processing traumas in the plaer's own pace, if the rest of the table is okay with that and with the recommendation of a professional. I'm not saying &quot;x-card is the devil, burn it!&quot;, but yes, i'm saying we should be wary with it and the like of it, because it's a slippery slope and I'm standing by that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The expectation that an x card is a ban on material is wrong. It is a notice that 'this hit harder than expected, can we regroup for a second?' The group can then decide how to proceed. It is not 'I dislike &lt;x&gt;, ban it', it is 'as a mature adult, playing a game with other mature adults, I'm finding it difficult to have fun with &lt;x&gt; involved. Can we discuss this and figure out how to proceed?' </div> </div> </div>Admittedly, I'm not an expert on the x-card, but everything I read says it's explicitly not that. It's not an asking for stopping and discussion (why would've need a card for that???), but a veto sign, without the need of explanation, or anything. It's just &quot;I don't want this/it's too much for me, please stop and/or change&quot;. But I could be wrong about it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T21:21:58-07:00","id":1153046,"title":"","content":"That's because most sources, quite frankly, use the x-card wrong and fail to address the entire range of uses. It's basic use is as an indicator that 'yo, hold up, I need to take a moment', and most sources leave it there. That's because in some cases, it may not be a possibility for there to be a discussion about why a halt needed to be called due to the private nature of trauma, but treating it as a universal 'BAN THIS' indicator is misusing it in the same way people have misused trigger warnings.<br /> <br /> Here are the ideal scenarios.<br /> 1. Something occurs and an x-card is dropped, and the reason why is not clear. The game pauses, and the ST takes a moment aside with the player. 'Are you alright?' 'Yes, I just need a minute, this is very rough because &lt;x&gt;, but then we can keep going now I know to expect it and I've had a chance to take a moment and get some distance'.<br /> 2. Something occurs and an x-card is dropped, and the reason why is not clear. The game pauses and the ST takes a moment aside with the player. 'You okay?' 'No, and I don't want to/cannot say why.' The ST accepts, moves the scene along away from the issue as much as possible, or if necessary calls a halt to the session. This is only an appropriate use of the card if the trauma involved is serious and personal or covered by a confidentiality requirement, but the reason it is treated as the default scenario is because you shouldn't pry into someone's private shit unless it's important, and a tabletop game is not. The appropriate response to this is 'okay, what do we need to do to make you okay right now?'<br /> 3. Something occurs and an x-card is dropped, and the reason why is not clear. The game pauses and the ST takes a moment aside with the player. 'You okay? What's wrong?' 'I can't handle &lt;x&gt; because it's way too close to &lt;a thing that happened, in whatever level of detail the person is comfortable with&gt; and I have some baggage there/i have a serious phobia of &lt;whatever&gt;. Can we adjust to avoid that in future?' 'Maybe, let's try and work it out and see where we go.'<br /> 4. Something occurs and an x-card is dropped. The ST knows why because it has been previously discussed (perhaps at an effective 'session zero' or privately or just through knowing the players well) or because the specific scene content is heavy even <i>within the context of the game*</i>, and smooths the scene on away from the cause. The game continues smoothly. This is the ideal outcome and usage scenario because it prevents the need to slow the game down, but it is far from the only one.<br /> <br /> (*: what does that mean? In Wraith, it would mean not so much 'a suicide' as 'extremely detailed descriptions of the suicide'. This is because the context of the game is important in determining what is or is not expected and reasonable.)<br /> <br /> Only in one of those usage scenarios is it a straight up 'whoah, no, never, not ever' veto. That one unfortunately is treated as the only one for simplicity by too many sources. It's also why more than a really brief sidebar is actually a good idea, since x cards are actually far more useful than that with more varied usage scenarios. Basically, in the same way that the other players and the ST have a responsibility to treat the emotional wellbeing of each other seriously, the person dropping the x-card has a obligation to use it responsibly. The individual circumstances of their life will determine which usage scenario is appropriate, and it very well may be number 2 - but it may also be 1, 3, or 4 just as easily and just as validly. Scenario 2 is especially applicable however to groups that don't know each other well.<br /> <br /> So, why the emphasis elsewhere on usage scenario 2? It's because a hell of a lot of people with deep-seated and serious traumas need to have that as an option - an ability to just say 'no'. But advocates for that are not saying it should be employed willy nilly. It's about things like 'I can't talk about this without bringing up serious emotional baggage no one here wants to deal with, myself included'. It is an extremely limited usage scenario that fundamentally diminishes the actual utility of the x-card, but which is emphasized in order to make it clear to people that 'no, and I do not want to/cannot discuss why' is an acceptable response when dealing with serious trauma. It is not the only usage scenario, and the card concept is not designed to lump every usage scenario under that one response banner but rather to ideally be used in conjunction with prior 'heads up' notices regarding content where possible.<br /> <br /> Basically, so far the discussions elsewhere have been inconsistent, choosing to emphasize different aspects without considering all usage scenarios. It's why you get some weird situations like 'this is just boring' being grounds for an x-card in some discussions of them (usually paired with the opposite 'o card' for 'more please') that cannot be questioned, because they aren't addressing different usage scenarios and the different natures of the tools and are trying to apply a serious tool to something it, quite frankly, should not be used for. X cards are appropriate for either serious traumas or touchy subjects generally like child molestation, and should be used and respected as such.<br /> <br /> Think of it this way. They exist to signal discomfort. If you know what the discomfort is as an ST, you just move on over it and adapt accordingly. If you don't, then the appropriate response is a check in with the player - preferably out of earshot for privacy reasons, though this is not always the case - and they may or may not disclose why. The appropriate contexts for their use will be decided by the game and the players, by reference to the maturity of the players and of the game, and it is entirely possible that some people might use them inappropriately, just like some STs act inappropriately towards their players. Just like that latter scenario, it does not render them any less useful a tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T04:39:36-07:00","id":1153113,"title":"","content":"Well, there's no damage from an extra half-page of text, so sure, include them. <br /> <br /> Personally it feels like someone suggesting all cars come with an option to replace the lap and shoulder belt with a five-point safety harness. It is provably safer to do so, and I'm sure there's anecdotal evidence of cases where such a harness would have saved a life. You can even point out race car drivers, who run the greatest danger of a deadly accident and who already require these. <br /> <br /> And all I'm left with is a gut feeling of, &quot;I never really thought I needed that.&quot; But you can't argue against a safety device without becoming an asshole, no matter how much or how little additional safety it affords. And you can't express concern about cars someday being filled with bubble wrap and packing peanuts without indulging in a slippery slope fallacy. <br /> <br /> Maybe someone better than I at argumentation can express my uneasiness in less of a Pickett's-Charge sort of way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T04:47:46-07:00","id":1153115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153025#post1153025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ee my above post for more detail, but the premise here is not 'oh no, dark content'. It is the potential for the dark content to inadvertantly resemble actual traumatic experience. To use your suicide question, the pitch is not 'please ban suicide if a player finds it difficult' (quite frankly, I think most people on my side of the argument would agree that if someone is so severely affected that any discussion of suicide is a serious trigger, then Wraith is unlikely to be a solid fit for them until those issues are addressed), it is 'oh shit, it turns out John's dad killed himself in the exact same way as Tim's character and it's kind of fucking him up'. Suicide can remain in play, but the fine details can be adjusted to avoid it if the group thinks that's appropriate. Or, quite possibly, all that will be needed is for the game to take a beat, let John recover, and he might very well be fine going forward once it is no longer an unexpected shock.<br /> <br /> The expectation that an x card is a ban on material is wrong. It is a notice that 'this hit harder than expected, can we regroup for a second?' The group can then decide how to proceed. It is not 'I dislike &lt;x&gt;, ban it', it is 'as a mature adult, playing a game with other mature adults, I'm finding it difficult to have fun with &lt;x&gt; involved. Can we discuss this and figure out how to proceed?'</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to add to this that oftentimes some days are better than others; this is a known element of both mental and physical trauma. So John in this example may have even known this suicide was a part of Tim's character and said it was fine, and one day he himself is surprised to find that it is hitting him harder than he expected. Another day and it would be fine, but on this day it is an unexpected shock and he needs a moment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T05:31:23-07:00","id":1153128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153113#post1153113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there's no damage from an extra half-page of text, so sure, include them.<br /> <br /> Personally it feels like someone suggesting all cars come with an option to replace the lap and shoulder belt with a five-point safety harness. It is provably safer to do so, and I'm sure there's anecdotal evidence of cases where such a harness would have saved a life. You can even point out race car drivers, who run the greatest danger of a deadly accident and who already require these.<br /> <br /> And all I'm left with is a gut feeling of, &quot;I never really thought I needed that.&quot; But you can't argue against a safety device without becoming an asshole, no matter how much or how little additional safety it affords. And you can't express concern about cars someday being filled with bubble wrap and packing peanuts without indulging in a slippery slope fallacy.<br /> <br /> Maybe someone better than I at argumentation can express my uneasiness in less of a Pickett's-Charge sort of way.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this situation, it's more analogous to suggesting driver safety training as part of the learning permit process, or perhaps even just mandating that the regular lap-and-shoulder belt be made mandatory and not optional. It's also great that you don't think you need it - you very well may not. These tools are not necessarily going to be of use for every group in every session any more than any other ST tool is. I myself don't need to be told about Rule Zero in most books, but I'm sure some DM somewhere has never thought about it before he cracks open a book containing it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T07:05:47-07:00","id":1153155,"title":"","content":"I've been discussing the X-card elsewhere, especially the ambiguous reactions towards it, and here's some observations I've made so far about the current clash:<br /> <br /> First of all, the card is a <i>tool</i>. And tools can be used towards good or bad ends, using good or bad methods. Something to keep in mind - something that seems to occasionally be forgotten, with people attributing virtue or vice to the tool itself. This flexibility of usage means that different people will have both different ideas and different actual experience with usage. With that in mind:<br /> <br /> World of Darkness is generally a game where, as others have stated, discomfort, anxiety and a state of fear are expected; they're why the Personal Horror thing is brought up. So the game line caters to people who want to push their limits. And when pushing limits, some sort of ejection lever is highly recommended for emergencies, and most risk-acknowledging, willingly-playing participants will nod in agreement to that. But there's a nuance to that agreement.<br /> <br /> The nuance lies primarily in the weight of the decision to use it. So let's say I decided that the plane is about to crash, or the building is on fire, or the train needs to be stopped. I look at the ejection switch / fire alarm / train's emergency brake lever. &quot;In case of emergency, break glass and pull the lever&quot;, it says. I acknowledge the cost of pulling the lever. Should I do it, the plane will crash without the pilot / the people will drop what they're doing and exit the building / the train will grind to a half and nobody will commute on time. Should I pull it, I'll break the immersion for me and my co-players, let the narrative lose its momentum and so on. Both for me and for others. If I crash a plane / scare a whole building of employees / stop a train, and after the fact it turns out I did so without justification, I'll carry the consequences for misusing such a necessary tool. So both the presentation of the tool and the rules of usage thereof encourage treating it responsibly.<br /> <br /> However, the original <i>wording</i> of the X-Card seems very easy to read in a way that erases the above nuance and responsibility:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Stavropoulos</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cI\u2019d like your help. Your help to make this game fun for everyone. <u>If anything makes anyone uncomfortable in any way</u>\u2026 [ draw X on an index card ] \u2026just lift this card up, or simply tap it [ place card at the center of the table ]. You don\u2019t have to explain why. <u>It doesn't matter why.</u> When we lift or tap this card, we simply edit out anything X-Carded. And if there is ever an issue, anyone can call for a break and we can talk privately. I know it sounds funny but it will help us play amazing games together and usually I\u2019m the one who uses the X card to protect myself from all of you! Please help make this game fun for everyone. Thank you!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Statements such as &quot;uncomfortable <u>in any way</u>&quot; and &quot;doesn't matter why&quot; are very easy to read as meaning that (a) the card is to be used lightly - not as an emergency break behind glass, but as a button one pushes with as little regard as when spending WP or the like and (b) that there is no place for evaluating whether the use is appropriate or not. Hopefully it's understandable why immersion-oriented, thrill-seeking people may have objections to both points a and b.<br /> <br /> Now, emphasise again that the <i>existence</i> of an emergency red lever behind a glass is a good thing on its own, as anyone may end up in a situation where it's needed. But the way the card is introduced makes it look like a thing that's less about needs and more about wants, and thus runs into the topic of whether [mis]use runs the risk of ruining the fun for everyone present.<br /> <br /> On a matter of personal opinion, of the safety tools I can recall offhand, other ones seem better designed and/or more nuanced than the card. Discussion of/agreement about things to avoid, red/yellow/green three-card system, veils and lines - they all seem more nuanced and more well-designed by comparison. Instead, the more frivolous interpretation of the X-card (but one that seems to match the letter of the card-rule) seems to be attracting enough negative attention to cast a shadow on the whole group of tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T08:40:16-07:00","id":1153183,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12622_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12622\" data-vbnamecard=\"12622\">vicky_molokh</a> , very well said, thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T09:53:43-07:00","id":1153208,"title":"","content":"No one is going to take away your fun because a few pages worth of &quot;here's how to deal with potentially stressful content and situations that may arise&quot; get added to a book. <br /> <br /> I've been running Vampire with someone who played for years before and for years after. He loves the game. He is a huge fan of horror movies, horror novels, etc. But he decided to go hunting one game session, on a dark and mostly-empty road. Succeeded, and decided he <i>really</i> needed to top off his Blood Pool. I told him he found a woman alone in a minivan that had broken down on the shoulder, trying to call a tow truck. He stopped, offered to help, then ambushed her and drained 8BP, which killed her. He staged it to look like an accident with the car. After all that, I made him roll Conscience and he got a bunch of successes. His character felt <i>awful</i> about what had happened, but kept his Humanity rating (it was kinda low, too, like 5?). So I described how he couldn't get the image out of his mind of her kids waiting at home, and how their mother would never get home. They'd just be waiting, and waiting, and she'd never come home. They'd never see her again. I said that as he'd arranged the &quot;accident&quot; scene, he'd found a photo of the kids in the minivan, and some of their toys. <br /> <br /> He had to stop playing that night. It was too much, and it stressed him out, so we called a stop to the session. The game continued next week, no real problems. And he's played VtM for years since. <br /> <br /> A lot of WoD Storytellers like to get graphic, and like to get emotional. They want to really stick the horror to you, and make you uncomfortable. That can <i>easily</i> go too far, even for people who love horror as a genre. Because it can <i>very</i> quickly get personal, especially in a group that knows each other. You may not be <i>intending</i> to make someone upset, but if you know a lot about their past and what scares them, or makes them worry, you can go too far without meaning to, just because you want to make it really creepy. <br /> <br /> It's not asking too much for a <i>horror game</i> to include information on how to manage <i>horror</i> properly. And properly managed horror <i>games</i> are still about having fun. There's a huge difference between watching a well-made horror film, and just watching footage of atrocities. One is enjoyable. The other makes you sick. We want to stick to the enjoyable part. If we're making our <i>friends</i> sick, we have a problem. And there is <i>plenty</i> of material that can <i>easily</i> be included in the game to help players avoid that as they learn how to manage horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T11:56:31-07:00","id":1153239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153208#post1153208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one is going to take away your fun because a few pages worth of &quot;here's how to deal with potentially stressful content and situations that may arise&quot; get added to a book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just not that simple and the whole debacle has deeper, long-term implications and honestly, I know a lot of people here won't agree with me, but I see where this kind of thing <i>could</i> lead, if getting out of hand and becoming pervasive and toxic, I just have to take a look at USA campuses. So, okay, there are situations where it could be very good to have it, then use it, by all means if you feel necessary! I'm not against reasonable usage, but in general, I'm very wary about this kind of things.<br /> <br /> Also no, I don't want pages upon pages sacrificed for that, it's not the goal of the book. In a WoD book, I want WoD-specific content and the absolutely necessary amount of general content for new STs (and they already had a room for &quot;please don't traumatize your players&quot; text, so adding this at the bare minimum is a logical step). Again, include it, write down the basics and then point the reader to targeted publications, just like WoD always did with history and local lore, for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not asking too much for a <i>horror game</i> to include information on how to manage <i>horror</i> properly. And properly managed horror <i>games</i> are still about having fun. There's a huge difference between watching a well-made horror film, and just watching footage of atrocities. One is enjoyable. The other makes you sick. We want to stick to the enjoyable part. If we're making our <i>friends</i> sick, we have a problem. And there is <i>plenty</i> of material that can <i>easily</i> be included in the game to help players avoid that as they learn how to manage horror. </div> </div> </div>Thing is, not everyone could handle, or even like horror films. When a group watches a horror film and one of them stops the film the fifth time and asking to skip an otherwise important or atmospheric scene, well, that becomes annoying, after a while. Maybe it'd be better to watch a less gruesome one at first?<br /> <br /> Just like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12622_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12622\" data-vbnamecard=\"12622\">vicky_molokh</a> wrote above, if it's an emergency brake and used only when absolutely necessary, then it's okay, but it could be too much quite easily and the original description doesn't really do much to alleviate those worries. That's why I'm saying it's okay, but I'm wary about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 10-26-2017, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T14:04:53-07:00","id":1153276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153239#post1153239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just not that simple and the whole debacle has deeper, long-term implications and honestly, I know a lot of people here won't agree with me, but I see where this kind of thing <i>could</i> lead, if getting out of hand and becoming pervasive and toxic, I just have to take a look at USA campuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does this have to do with the current discussion? Why are you trying to start a political fight and drag the thread down?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T14:31:36-07:00","id":1153285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153276#post1153276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What does this have to do with the current discussion? Why are you trying to start a political fight and drag the thread down?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed everyone here could recognize a not-exactly-in-topic-but-working-along (debatably)-similar-lines-as-a-parallel example. My opinion is that parallels could be drawn in the thought processes behind the campus-safe-space debacle and the x-card and the former could be used as an example to highlight the possible dangers with the later, if used too excessively and letting it go out of hand and in general, the possible problems with that kind of thinking.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I'm not interested in a political fight and honestly, I'm sad I've had to explain this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 10-26-2017, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T18:00:52-07:00","id":1153344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153239#post1153239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's just not that simple and the whole debacle has deeper, long-term implications and honestly, I know a lot of people here won't agree with me, but I see where this kind of thing <i>could</i> lead, if getting out of hand and becoming pervasive and toxic, I just have to take a look at USA campuses. So, okay, there are situations where it could be very good to have it, then use it, by all means if you feel necessary! I'm not against reasonable usage, but in general, I'm very wary about this kind of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prove it. Show the projected slope, show the underlying logic and rationale, show that the situation is comparable to USA campuses as opposed to say, the BDSM scene where coded safewords and degrees of progression are a long-accepted standard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also no, I don't want pages upon pages sacrificed for that, it's not the goal of the book. In a WoD book, I want WoD-specific content and the absolutely necessary amount of general content for new STs (and they already had a room for &quot;please don't traumatize your players&quot; text, so adding this at the bare minimum is a logical step). Again, include it, write down the basics and then point the reader to targeted publications, just like WoD always did with history and local lore, for example. </div> </div> </div>We already sacrifice pages upon pages for ST advice in core books. This is no different in that regard to content that is already present.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thing is, not everyone could handle, or even like horror films. When a group watches a horror film and one of them stops the film the fifth time and asking to skip an otherwise important or atmospheric scene, well, that becomes annoying, after a while. Maybe it'd be better to watch a less gruesome one at first? </div> </div> </div>You assume, erroneously, that these tools are intended to in some way abrogate the responsibility of players and groups to choose content that is appropriate. It is very much not that. It is, in the context we are proposing and the formulation we are proposing, designed to provide an augmentive mechanism to that basic responsibility. Again - not one of us is advocating that people should just blindly storm in to Wraith without regard to whether or not they like the premise or that people who find the game consistently triggering without some special circumstance should continue to play it.<br /> <br /> We are advocating for a set of tools that mean that people who have specific triggers not opposed to the general game itself be able to easily indicate when something, in the most mature game of the setting with the most likelihood of resembling actual traumatic events, is causing them difficulty. This does not then mean that we're suggesting they 'stop the film a fifth time' - we're suggesting that a tool be in place if they need to stop it the first time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12622_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12622\" data-vbnamecard=\"12622\">vicky_molokh</a> wrote above, if it's an emergency brake and used only when absolutely necessary, then it's okay, but it could be too much quite easily and the original description doesn't really do much to alleviate those worries. That's why I'm saying it's okay, but I'm wary about it. </div> </div> </div>That's why I'm advocating for a revised description, which I took great pains to explain and which I'm fairly sure most advocates for X cards in mature games aimed at mature audiences would agree is a better fit. And let me just point something out.<br /> <br /> Your worst case scenario of it being used too easily? There is literally nothing stopping that from happening at your table right now, in the form of a player just going 'no, fuck this game' every ten minutes. The same basic level of trust we give our other players - that they aren't going to, in bad faith, disrupt the flow of the game (or in a friends game, they might, but in a way that everyone can enjoy) - will still apply. These tools do not alter it. If you can't trust people not to abuse them, you can't trust them not to disrupt the flow of the game in a hundred other ways.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T18:02:18-07:00","id":1153349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153285#post1153285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assumed everyone here could recognize a not-exactly-in-topic-but-working-along (debatably)-similar-lines-as-a-parallel example. My opinion is that parallels could be drawn in the thought processes behind the campus-safe-space debacle and the x-card and the former could be used as an example to highlight the possible dangers with the later, if used too excessively and letting it go out of hand and in general, the possible problems with that kind of thinking.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I'm not interested in a political fight and honestly, I'm sad I've had to explain this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, show the situation is actually analogous and that the comparison to a situation where the concepts are abused and misrepresented - something that more words clarifying intent can help remedy, in direct counter to your 'a tiny sidebar is fine' mentality - is more apt than the closer analogy of BDSM community safewords.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T18:05:53-07:00","id":1153350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153155#post1153155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been discussing the X-card elsewhere, especially the ambiguous reactions towards it, and here's some observations I've made so far about the current clash:<br /> <br /> First of all, the card is a <i>tool</i>. And tools can be used towards good or bad ends, using good or bad methods. Something to keep in mind - something that seems to occasionally be forgotten, with people attributing virtue or vice to the tool itself. This flexibility of usage means that different people will have both different ideas and different actual experience with usage. With that in mind:<br /> <br /> World of Darkness is generally a game where, as others have stated, discomfort, anxiety and a state of fear are expected; they're why the Personal Horror thing is brought up. So the game line caters to people who want to push their limits. And when pushing limits, some sort of ejection lever is highly recommended for emergencies, and most risk-acknowledging, willingly-playing participants will nod in agreement to that. But there's a nuance to that agreement.<br /> <br /> The nuance lies primarily in the weight of the decision to use it. So let's say I decided that the plane is about to crash, or the building is on fire, or the train needs to be stopped. I look at the ejection switch / fire alarm / train's emergency brake lever. &quot;In case of emergency, break glass and pull the lever&quot;, it says. I acknowledge the cost of pulling the lever. Should I do it, the plane will crash without the pilot / the people will drop what they're doing and exit the building / the train will grind to a half and nobody will commute on time. Should I pull it, I'll break the immersion for me and my co-players, let the narrative lose its momentum and so on. Both for me and for others. If I crash a plane / scare a whole building of employees / stop a train, and after the fact it turns out I did so without justification, I'll carry the consequences for misusing such a necessary tool. So both the presentation of the tool and the rules of usage thereof encourage treating it responsibly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe we are in agreement on these basic points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, the original <i>wording</i> of the X-Card seems very easy to read in a way that erases the above nuance and responsibility:<br /> <br /> Statements such as &quot;uncomfortable <u>in any way</u>&quot; and &quot;doesn't matter why&quot; are very easy to read as meaning that (a) the card is to be used lightly - not as an emergency break behind glass, but as a button one pushes with as little regard as when spending WP or the like and (b) that there is no place for evaluating whether the use is appropriate or not. Hopefully it's understandable why immersion-oriented, thrill-seeking people may have objections to both points a and b. </div> </div> </div>I believe we are still in agreement, and it is the poor design of the original concept that I spent quite some time remedying upthread. Most usage scenarios address only one possible use while trying to map the concept to a very broad range of possibilities, with the result being a mismatch for the context of Wraith. That does not mean the card concept does not have merit - it just needs to be tailored to the context, just like most everything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, emphasise again that the <i>existence</i> of an emergency red lever behind a glass is a good thing on its own, as anyone may end up in a situation where it's needed. But the way the card is introduced makes it look like a thing that's less about needs and more about wants, and thus runs into the topic of whether [mis]use runs the risk of ruining the fun for everyone present.<br /> <br /> On a matter of personal opinion, of the safety tools I can recall offhand, other ones seem better designed and/or more nuanced than the card. Discussion of/agreement about things to avoid, red/yellow/green three-card system, veils and lines - they all seem more nuanced and more well-designed by comparison. Instead, the more frivolous interpretation of the X-card (but one that seems to match the letter of the card-rule) seems to be attracting enough negative attention to cast a shadow on the whole group of tools. </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately so. Personally, I feel that the three card system is a little much for Wraith but I can see the merit. Veils and lines are also fine tools. Mostly I focus on the card as a point of debate as the same uses can be reasoned by analogy for the lines and veils, and a defence of the more heavily questioned tool tends to encompass concerns and fears around the less contentious ones.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T09:45:07-07:00","id":1153510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153022#post1153022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gotta say alot of what i'm seeing here is making me interested in wraith. Is it the next 'something20' to come out? And if not would it be worth it to get the last corebook? (apologies if this isnt the right thread to ask this)</div> </div> </div> </div>The wait on Wraith20 is interminable. It was solicited long before Changeling20 and isn't out yet (so that makes it a few YEARS since the Kickstarter), and, despite what you may read on other threads, there is no actual firm or even tentative date for it to come out. It's listed as being &quot;In Proofing&quot; and that has been taken as a sign that it will come out soon, but that's pretty much false optimism, as it has been there and not there at about that point for a very long time, coming onto the list under &quot;Art Direction&quot; or &quot;Proofing&quot; than vanishing altogether for weeks at a time. Considering the hold up seems to be what it always has, which is Dansky's ability to commit time to completing the project for various reasons (alternatively REALLY good and just plain ehhhh....) .<br /> <br /> So if you are waiting for Wraith20 to take a look, it's very much a backburner thing what will probably be a delightful surprise some day in the future.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, pretty much all the subject matter of the game that is behind this thread is in the game proper, and the pdf version is available on sale at Drivethru for substantial savings up through Halloween. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T09:53:07-07:00","id":1153515,"title":"","content":"I backed it on Kickstarter for a PDF copy, and stopped reading the updates months ago. It has moved at a glacial pace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T10:03:17-07:00","id":1153519,"title":"","content":"But let's take a second here and touch on this &quot;campus safe space debacle&quot;. Because that's exactly what gaming should be: a safe space. An environment where you can join a group dedicating to having <i>fun</i> together as a team, without attacking other people, causing anyone distress, or being hurtful. You know, the way most friend groups operate. Because if your friends insult you, cause you distress, verbally harass you, make fun of your choices, and attack you... your friends aren't your friends. They're pathetic little pus-sucking dickfish. <br /> <br /> If you take your <i>friends</i> to see a horror movie, and one of them starts to freak out in the middle of it, obviously in distress.. what do you do? Ignore them? Sigh unhappily and ask them to leave so you can continue enjoying the movie? Complain afterwards that they ruined the movie for you? You might be an awful person if those are your reactions. This is your <i>friend</i>. And they're upset. The movie is not more important. <br /> <br /> We are not talking about a situation where you have five friends, four of whom love horror movies and one of whom hates them, but wants to hang out anyway, so you never ever get to watch a horror movie, EVER AGAIN. We are talking about you having five friends, ALL of whom love horror movies, and there is a problem with THIS scene, in THIS movie, causing one friend distress.<br /> <br /> Sit down on your slippery slope to censorship blandland. That's never going to happen. You don't need to defend against basic human decency just to preserve your right to enjoy edgy things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T10:10:48-07:00","id":1153523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153510#post1153510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if you are waiting for Wraith20 to take a look, it's very much a backburner thing what will probably be a delightful surprise some day in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thx, i had try to look, but everything i saw seemed to imply it would be out soon. I didnt realise that 'soon' has been implied for a long time now.<br /> Maybe its just as well, my funds are low at the moment so waiting a bit might be good thing in the end :P<br /> I'll put Wraith20 in my 'ideas for a future game' folder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T11:20:33-07:00","id":1153539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153344#post1153344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prove it. Show the projected slope, show the underlying logic and rationale, show that the situation is comparable to USA campuses as opposed to say, the BDSM scene where coded safewords and degrees of progression are a long-accepted standard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, come on! Prove what? That the notion of &quot;participant safety&quot; and &quot;safety mechanisms&quot; could be used sensibly (BDSM, Nordic LARP), but could be abused too (campuses)?<br /> <br /> You're trying to frame me as if I've opposed the very concept of x-card. I didn't. I said, include it in the book and use it, if needed, but use it with care. And also, yes, I'm wary about safety tools in general, not because they're a bad thing on themselves (they're not, they could be very useful), but because they're part of a greater trend. Maybe it's just in my mind, maybe I'm drawing connections which aren't there, but honestly, I don't think so. Prove it? sorry, I don't have the scientific tools and knowledge to prove the very subtle and tangential connections between various phenomenon, but the sum of them conveys to me a shift in trends which I could perceive and some of those trends I don't like. So yes, I'll be wary about every part of those trends. Not against them, on principle just like I'm not against the x-card, but careful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We already sacrifice pages upon pages for ST advice in core books. This is no different in that regard to content that is already present. </div> </div> </div>For absolutely necessary basic general ST advice and WoD-specific ones. To me, discussing the x-card in length (multiple pages) is neither, but you're very welcome to disagree.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You assume, erroneously, that these tools are intended to in some way abrogate the responsibility of players and groups to choose content that is appropriate. It is very much not that. It is, in the context we are proposing and the formulation we are proposing, designed to provide an augmentive mechanism to that basic responsibility. Again - not one of us is advocating that people should just blindly storm in to Wraith without regard to whether or not they like the premise or that people who find the game consistently triggering without some special circumstance should continue to play it.<br /> <br /> We are advocating for a set of tools that mean that people who have specific triggers not opposed to the general game itself be able to easily indicate when something, in the most mature game of the setting with the most likelihood of resembling actual traumatic events, is causing them difficulty. This does not then mean that we're suggesting they 'stop the film a fifth time' - we're suggesting that a tool be in place if they need to stop it the first time. </div> </div> </div>Every tool and good intention could be abused. I'm still not sayin it doesn't have it's place and needed sometimes, for some people, I'm just wary of the potential for overusing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why I'm advocating for a revised description, which I took great pains to explain and which I'm fairly sure most advocates for X cards in mature games aimed at mature audiences would agree is a better fit. And let me just point something out. </div> </div> </div>Actually, I had zero problems with your description. I'd welcome something like that, in that length in the book. That's sensible and still under one page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your worst case scenario of it being used too easily? There is literally nothing stopping that from happening at your table right now, in the form of a player just going 'no, fuck this game' every ten minutes. </div> </div> </div>After which everyone would shout &quot;well, show the fucking door to yourself&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The same basic level of trust we give our other players - that they aren't going to, in bad faith, disrupt the flow of the game (or in a friends game, they might, but in a way that everyone can enjoy) - will still apply. These tools do not alter it. If you can't trust people not to abuse them, you can't trust them not to disrupt the flow of the game in a hundred other ways. </div> </div> </div>That's not so simple with strangers, which is, I think the main situation where the x-card was being advocated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, show the situation is actually analogous and that the comparison to a situation where the concepts are abused and misrepresented - something that more words clarifying intent can help remedy, in direct counter to your 'a tiny sidebar is fine' mentality - is more apt than the closer analogy of BDSM community safewords. </div> </div> </div>I never said &quot;tiny sidebar&quot;, I said sidebar, or a column of text. A column could be a half-page even and WoD books had some pretty lengthy sidebars. I'd be okay with spending a page at maximum on this. But no, I still don't want pages upon pages of description about using it in a WoD corebook. Maybe in a dedicated ST companion/handbook, but since, again, there are targeted publications for the x-card and other safety tools, I'd rather see more WoD and the game in question specific ST stuff than this. I'm perfectly happy with what WoD book ever said: &quot;we are pointing you to the direction of certain things, so go and do your research!&quot;<br /> <br /> As I said, I liked your description, you did a good job remedying the concept. However, sorry, but the original description (which is known by most people) is screaming &quot;safe space&quot; to me. Actually, I assume you didn't like it either, since as you said, you spent a lot of time writing a better description<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 10-27-2017, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T11:24:08-07:00","id":1153541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153519#post1153519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But let's take a second here and touch on this &quot;campus safe space debacle&quot;. Because that's exactly what gaming should be: a safe space. An environment where you can join a group dedicating to having <i>fun</i> together as a team, without attacking other people, causing anyone distress, or being hurtful. You know, the way most friend groups operate. Because if your friends insult you, cause you distress, verbally harass you, make fun of your choices, and attack you... your friends aren't your friends. They're pathetic little pus-sucking dickfish.<br /> <br /> If you take your <i>friends</i> to see a horror movie, and one of them starts to freak out in the middle of it, obviously in distress.. what do you do? Ignore them? Sigh unhappily and ask them to leave so you can continue enjoying the movie? Complain afterwards that they ruined the movie for you? You might be an awful person if those are your reactions. This is your <i>friend</i>. And they're upset. The movie is not more important.<br /> <br /> We are not talking about a situation where you have five friends, four of whom love horror movies and one of whom hates them, but wants to hang out anyway, so you never ever get to watch a horror movie, EVER AGAIN. We are talking about you having five friends, ALL of whom love horror movies, and there is a problem with THIS scene, in THIS movie, causing one friend distress.<br /> <br /> Sit down on your slippery slope to censorship blandland. That's never going to happen. You don't need to defend against basic human decency just to preserve your right to enjoy edgy things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, no, totally not worth my time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Have a nice day! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T18:57:29-07:00","id":1153638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153539#post1153539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh, come on! Prove what? That the notion of &quot;participant safety&quot; and &quot;safety mechanisms&quot; could be used sensibly (BDSM, Nordic LARP), but could be abused too (campuses)?<br /> <br /> You're trying to frame me as if I've opposed the very concept of x-card. I didn't. I said, include it in the book and use it, if needed, but use it with care. And also, yes, I'm wary about safety tools in general, not because they're a bad thing on themselves (they're not, they could be very useful), but because they're part of a greater trend. Maybe it's just in my mind, maybe I'm drawing connections which aren't there, but honestly, I don't think so. Prove it? sorry, I don't have the scientific tools and knowledge to prove the very subtle and tangential connections between various phenomenon, but the sum of them conveys to me a shift in trends which I could perceive and some of those trends I don't like. So yes, I'll be wary about every part of those trends. Not against them, on principle just like I'm not against the x-card, but careful.</div> </div> </div> </div>You continue to advance a theory that this is in some way part of a slippery slope. That undercuts your stance of 'no the tool is good but careful' into a backdoor attack, and you know it. If you can't actually show that this situation is more analogous to the perceived political correctness crisis of college campuses than it is to BDSM safewords, then maybe stop drawing those connections and arguing them in a public forum where people are entitled to ask you to back up and defend your arguments.<br /> <br /> Basically, put up or shut up, and either demonstrate your slippery slope is not fallacious or stop trying to argue it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For absolutely necessary basic general ST advice and WoD-specific ones. To me, discussing the x-card in length (multiple pages) is neither, but you're very welcome to disagree. </div> </div> </div>Wraith is a game about mature themes, involving very dark content. Tools that have proven useful - and to be clear, the multiple page discussion would be of more than one - for that style of game are very much general ST advice and WoD-specific advice. It falls into both categories. Can you explain why it doesn't?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every tool and good intention could be abused. I'm still not sayin it doesn't have it's place and needed sometimes, for some people, I'm just wary of the potential for overusing it. </div> </div> </div>We return again to your backdoor attempts to argue against the concept. As you say, every tool can be abused - is there a reason you have chosen only these ones to argue against, and not the other suites of ST tools?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, I had zero problems with your description. I'd welcome something like that, in that length in the book. That's sensible and still under one page. </div> </div> </div>Great. Is there a reason you continue, then, to argue about slippery slopes and overuse?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After which everyone would shout &quot;well, show the fucking door to yourself&quot;. </div> </div> </div>And the same practical element applies here. No part of these tools prevents a group from not inviting someone who habitually misuses them back to the group. Certainly, you might get a lot more side eye over it from other groups, but if the case is actually of someone misusing the tool those other groups'll be fairly easy to explain the situation to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not so simple with strangers, which is, I think the main situation where the x-card was being advocated. </div> </div> </div>If you cannot give basic good faith to a new group of players, there are far bigger problems at that table than the potential misuse of an x-card.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I never said &quot;tiny sidebar&quot;, I said sidebar, or a column of text. A column could be a half-page even and WoD books had some pretty lengthy sidebars. I'd be okay with spending a page at maximum on this. But no, I still don't want pages upon pages of description about using it in a WoD corebook. Maybe in a dedicated ST companion/handbook, but since, again, there are targeted publications for the x-card and other safety tools, I'd rather see more WoD and the game in question specific ST stuff than this. I'm perfectly happy with what WoD book ever said: &quot;we are pointing you to the direction of certain things, so go and do your research!&quot; </div> </div> </div>You're quite right you never specified tiny sidebar. However, the amazing thing about words is they can imply meaning to other words, and your ranting and raving about 'edge' and 'castration' and 'don't take up much space' together contribute to two views. First, you do not actually want the tools to be put in place. Second, if they must be, you would prefer the bare minimum treatment.<br /> <br /> This is also why I have trouble taking your 'no, the tools are fine!' stance seriously. When you continuously undercut the intention of the statement by complaining about the risk of abuse, or how people want to play WoD 'without the implications', the actual contextual reading is 'I am paying lip service to an idea that I am in fact opposed to.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I said, I liked your description, you did a good job remedying the concept. However, sorry, but the original description (which is known by most people) is screaming &quot;safe space&quot; to me. Actually, I assume you didn't like it either, since as you said, you spent a lot of time writing a better description </div> </div> </div>Are you familiar with what the term 'safe space' actually entails and means, outside of its recent misuse by fuckwits? If not, I am happy to explain its actual roots and purposes to you. Like a lot of actually quite useful concepts (privilege, for instance), there's been a dilution of meaning by a fringe on one side and an amplification of the misuse cases by the other fringe to try and discredit the entire concept.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T20:48:57-07:00","id":1153659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153519#post1153519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But let's take a second here and touch on this &quot;campus safe space debacle&quot;. Because that's exactly what gaming should be: a safe space. An environment where you can join a group dedicating to having <i>fun</i> together as a team, without attacking other people, causing anyone distress, or being hurtful. You know, the way most friend groups operate. Because if your friends insult you, cause you distress, verbally harass you, make fun of your choices, and attack you... your friends aren't your friends. They're pathetic little pus-sucking dickfish.<br /> <br /> If you take your <i>friends</i> to see a horror movie, and one of them starts to freak out in the middle of it, obviously in distress.. what do you do? Ignore them? Sigh unhappily and ask them to leave so you can continue enjoying the movie? Complain afterwards that they ruined the movie for you? You might be an awful person if those are your reactions. This is your <i>friend</i>. And they're upset. The movie is not more important.<br /> <br /> We are not talking about a situation where you have five friends, four of whom love horror movies and one of whom hates them, but wants to hang out anyway, so you never ever get to watch a horror movie, EVER AGAIN. We are talking about you having five friends, ALL of whom love horror movies, and there is a problem with THIS scene, in THIS movie, causing one friend distress.<br /> <br /> Sit down on your slippery slope to censorship blandland. That's never going to happen. You don't need to defend against basic human decency just to preserve your right to enjoy edgy things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T00:37:07-07:00","id":1153688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153349#post1153349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, show the situation is actually analogous and that the comparison to a situation where the concepts are abused and misrepresented - something that more words clarifying intent can help remedy, in direct counter to your 'a tiny sidebar is fine' mentality - is more apt than the closer analogy of BDSM community safewords.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quoting this because it's the most concise synopsis of your request, even though other recent posts go into the same branch of the topic. I think the part of the X-card document I quoted is sufficient proof that it's built in a way which nudges people towards using it in a way that prevents pushing one's limits (Demolition Man society), as opposed to a way which facilitates overcoming/transcending/expanding/etc. those limits (BDSM). Any sidebars that introduce safety mechanisms in a way similar to the X-card will have effects similar to the X-card. Sidebars should be written carefully, in a way that makes people keep the emergency medical aid on speeddial, <b>not</b> dial the emergency medical aid at the slightest discomfort.<br /> <br /> * == I'm using that instead of 'campus safespaces' because the 'campus safespace debate' seems to be a very culturally-NATO-specific or culturally-North-American-specific sort of thing (not sure which of the two).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12622,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","user":"vicky_molokh","date":". 10-28-2017, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T00:51:17-07:00","id":1153690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153688#post1153688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quoting this because it's the most concise synopsis of your request, even though other recent posts go into the same branch of the topic. I think the part of the X-card document I quoted is sufficient proof that it's built in a way which nudges people towards using it in a way that prevents pushing one's limits (Demolition Man society), as opposed to a way which facilitates overcoming/transcending/expanding/etc. those limits (BDSM). Any sidebars that introduce safety mechanisms in a way similar to the X-card will have effects similar to the X-card. Sidebars should be written carefully, in a way that makes people keep the emergency medical aid on speeddial, <b>not</b> dial the emergency medical aid at the slightest discomfort.<br /> <br /> * == I'm using that instead of 'campus safespaces' because the 'campus safespace debate' seems to be a very culturally-NATO-specific or culturally-North-American-specific sort of thing (not sure which of the two).</div> </div> </div> </div>And can you show that the formulations suggested by advocates in this thread are susceptible to the same problem? And, more importantly, that they are more susceptible to this than the use of other tools and that such a possibility's potential harm outweighs the potential good of the concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T00:55:03-07:00","id":1153691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153638#post1153638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You continue to advance a theory that this is in some way part of a slippery slope. That undercuts your stance of 'no the tool is good but careful' into a backdoor attack, and you know it. If you can't actually show that this situation is more analogous to the perceived political correctness crisis of college campuses than it is to BDSM safewords, then maybe stop drawing those connections and arguing them in a public forum where people are entitled to ask you to back up and defend your arguments.<br /> <br /> Basically, put up or shut up, and either demonstrate your slippery slope is not fallacious or stop trying to argue it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, you made up your mind about my stance, and at this point I can't do anything about it, so I won't spent much time arguing you further. Also, <i>again</i>, I can't show direct connections, because it's just a little element of the big picture, a trickle in the shifting of trends and attitudes about safety in gaming and those trends already changed how books were written, what content went into them, etc. and sometimes not for the better in my eyes. Safety is something you could always took too far, it's always a possibility and a danger.<br /> <br /> You could demand &quot;proof&quot; as much as you want, I won't provide hard data for you, because for one, it's a feeling, a hunch on my part and I'm not ashamed to say it and I already said that I ould be on the wrong and also, I'm not an expert on social sciences (and also, not a native English speaker), so I'm drawing conclusions on impressions and yes those could lead astray.<br /> <br /> Also, you're continuously misrepresenting my stance on the topic, because I never wrote that it's <i>more</i> like campuses than safewords. I explicitly said, just in the last post, that, when using sensibly, it's like the later, but when overused (and frankly, the original description conveys more an attitude like that toward the whole thing) it's more akin to me to the former.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wraith is a game about mature themes, involving very dark content. Tools that have proven useful - and to be clear, the multiple page discussion would be of more than one - for that style of game are very much general ST advice and WoD-specific advice. It falls into both categories. Can you explain why it doesn't? </div> </div> </div>I said you're welcome to disagree. It's just not an essential general tool to me, but one for extreme occasions. There are tons of ST advice and tools that don't get multiple pages of description in a corebook, but just a column, because of limited space and in favor of the essential generalities for new STs and some WoD and game-specific advice. For example, in V20, most columns in the ST section are one and a half pages long at best, but msot are between half-a-page to 3/4 a page. I'm not seeing this as more important than those. Ketchup is an essential ingredient for pizza for some, it's not for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We return again to your backdoor attempts to argue against the concept. As you say, every tool can be abused - is there a reason you have chosen only these ones to argue against, and not the other suites of ST tools? </div> </div> </div>Yes, because I'm still seeing them as a part of a bigger trend and also because these tools are new additions to gaming and it's always prudent to be careful with new stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Great. Is there a reason you continue, then, to argue about slippery slopes and overuse? </div> </div> </div>How exactly your specific description which I liked should lead to change my whole view on this?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the same practical element applies here. No part of these tools prevents a group from not inviting someone who habitually misuses them back to the group. Certainly, you might get a lot more side eye over it from other groups, but if the case is actually of someone misusing the tool those other groups'll be fairly easy to explain the situation to. </div> </div> </div>But the original description leaves a lot more room for overuse in the wording, although not necessiates it. If you're halting the game in the usual way, that'll lead to questions, to asking for explanations, etc. The original wording of the card doesn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you cannot give basic good faith to a new group of players, there are far bigger problems at that table than the potential misuse of an x-card. </div> </div> </div>And if you can't give basic good faith to a group of players that they'll respect you f you simply say &quot;please stop this&quot;, without a card and its &quot;rules&quot; giving you an actual emergency break, then I'd say there are much bigger problems than the absence of the card.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're quite right you never specified tiny sidebar. However, the amazing thing about words is they can imply meaning to other words, and your ranting and raving about 'edge' and 'castration' and 'don't take up much space' together contribute to two views. First, you do not actually want the tools to be put in place. Second, if they must be, you would prefer the bare minimum treatment. </div> </div> </div>And the amazing things about humans is the extraordinary ability to see what they want to see, especially if they already made up their mind (and I have enough self-critique to say, I might be guilty in that, regarding the x-card being part of what I'm seeing as not-always positive trends), regardless of the actual information they're looking at. Maybe you might consider the notion that you misinterpreted my stance and stop being aggressive?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is also why I have trouble taking your 'no, the tools are fine!' stance seriously. When you continuously undercut the intention of the statement by complaining about the risk of abuse, or how people want to play WoD 'without the implications', the actual contextual reading is 'I am paying lip service to an idea that I am in fact opposed to.' </div> </div> </div>Also, it might be beneficial for you to stop thinking in polar extremes. Believe it or not, I'm perfectly capable of having an opinion about a given thing that includes positive, neutral and negative impressions and sides at the same time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you familiar with what the term 'safe space' actually entails and means, outside of its recent misuse by fuckwits? If not, I am happy to explain its actual roots and purposes to you. Like a lot of actually quite useful concepts (privilege, for instance), there's been a dilution of meaning by a fringe on one side and an amplification of the misuse cases by the other fringe to try and discredit the entire concept. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm familiar with that, thank you. You know, misuses are generally like that, good intentions and even ideas taken too far. That the original concept was/is something good doesn't redeem the extremities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 10-28-2017, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T01:01:59-07:00","id":1153692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153688#post1153688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quoting this because it's the most concise synopsis of your request, even though other recent posts go into the same branch of the topic. I think the part of the X-card document I quoted is sufficient proof that it's built in a way which nudges people towards using it in a way that prevents pushing one's limits (Demolition Man society), as opposed to a way which facilitates overcoming/transcending/expanding/etc. those limits (BDSM). Any sidebars that introduce safety mechanisms in a way similar to the X-card will have effects similar to the X-card. Sidebars should be written carefully, in a way that makes people keep the emergency medical aid on speeddial, <b>not</b> dial the emergency medical aid at the slightest discomfort.<br /> <br /> * == I'm using that instead of 'campus safespaces' because the 'campus safespace debate' seems to be a very culturally-NATO-specific or culturally-North-American-specific sort of thing (not sure which of the two).</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, thanks!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153690#post1153690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And can you show that the formulations suggested by advocates in this thread are susceptible to the same problem? And, more importantly, that they are more susceptible to this than the use of other tools and that such a possibility's potential harm outweighs the potential good of the concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, your version was good and you actually managed to warm me up more to the tool. I'd include that without a hitch in future books. But sorry, it's just a person's take on the subject in question, on a forum, not the original description, known by most (including me), which provided the basis for initial impressions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 10-28-2017, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T01:28:10-07:00","id":1153695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153690#post1153690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And can you show that the formulations suggested by advocates in this thread are susceptible to the same problem? And, more importantly, that they are more susceptible to this than the use of other tools and that such a possibility's potential harm outweighs the potential good of the concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a rather broad question, because different people post different formulations, and the formulations in actual books are likely to differ from formulations in forum posts. E.g. the post that talks about one scene in a film causing distress, while the whole point of horror films is causing distress and freaking out the audience for most of the film's duration, seems to be leaning closest to the formulation whose drawbacks I objected to (i.e. is leaning towards avoiding things that push one's limits). Of course, this is partially a matter of interpreting ambiguous words, which is a problem that goes in both directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T04:08:40-07:00","id":1153897,"title":"","content":"Regardless of, (and even that is debatable), the original intent or purpose for safe spaces, privilege, and similar jargon, these concepts have very distinct meanings now, and it is not &quot;recent&quot;. But that is irrelevent. Those things have changed into two mutually exclusive concepts, and everything in between, and are, factually, now ways to end discussions or debates when sides can not counter others or lack empathy to see other sides points of views or problems. (The exact thing they are, suppossedly, intended to prevent, right?) They are very loaded, hot-button concepts that have probably done much more harm to everyone than help, (cough, cough, privilege, cough).<br /> <br /> I am not oppossed to WW/OP including a reasonable discussion on things like this, but I am weary of the continued pressure towards a trend to soften things. A large part of the reason I am confortable with the WoD was the &quot;be a &quot;Fing&quot; adult&quot; mentality, and I think the best solution is to, right up front, for Wraith, say &quot;This is a game about death, torment, suffering, and corruption. It involves some pretty dark stuff, including slavery, murder, suicide, lose of control, temptation, and various religious concepts. Be warned, and if you would like to have some extra tools for play if things cut a little too close to home, here are a few web cites you can go for advice:<br /> A.)<br /> B.)<br /> C.)...&quot;<br /> <br /> I would even suggest a game setting neutral book, perhaps a free pdf or something that could discuss this for each game. Something like the April Fools Day releases, (size-wise, not because it is a joke), or Conversion Guides. That would allow for a lot more general discussion and have less need to watch page count, but would also not be an issue with taking up page space in the Wraith book itself, (which to be blunt, has already had too little setting and advice for the game on past editions).<br /> <br /> Something to consider, the ST Vault is a thing, and if you really want this tyoe of thing, or especially if you want, it seems change the meaning of X Cards, why not simply make it yourself and put it up on the Vault?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 10-29-2017, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T08:56:24-07:00","id":1153930,"title":"","content":"So far, this has all been gloriously abstract and philosophical, but, as I said to my high school calculus teacher, &quot;What's it good for?&quot;<br /> <br /> - Have any of the participants played or, even better, run Wraith games? Alternatively, other White Wolf games that deal with similar or equivalent issues? (Like Telgar's example from a Vampire game... Hi Telgar!)<br /> - Did they address these issues either as part of the game set-up, with the players and/or in game when things were on or above the table? <br /> - Did the group go into the game thinking that what they were doing was wrestling with dark issues as ersatz psychotherapy or that they were going to play a game with a group of friends for fun and either not think to address these issues or think about all this or think about it and not deal with it in any structured way?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that all this heady talk isn't as useful or even more useful than a sidebar or a block of text, but, practically, how does this go down in games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T09:41:59-07:00","id":1154148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153897#post1153897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of, (and even that is debatable), the original intent or purpose for safe spaces, privilege, and similar jargon, these concepts have very distinct meanings now, and it is not &quot;recent&quot;. But that is irrelevent. Those things have changed into two mutually exclusive concepts, and everything in between, and are, factually, now ways to end discussions or debates when sides can not counter others or lack empathy to see other sides points of views or problems. (The exact thing they are, suppossedly, intended to prevent, right?) They are very loaded, hot-button concepts that have probably done much more harm to everyone than help, (cough, cough, privilege, cough).<br /> <br /> I am not oppossed to WW/OP including a reasonable discussion on things like this, but I am weary of the continued pressure towards a trend to soften things. A large part of the reason I am confortable with the WoD was the &quot;be a &quot;Fing&quot; adult&quot; mentality, and I think the best solution is to, right up front, for Wraith, say &quot;This is a game about death, torment, suffering, and corruption. It involves some pretty dark stuff, including slavery, murder, suicide, lose of control, temptation, and various religious concepts. Be warned, and if you would like to have some extra tools for play if things cut a little too close to home, here are a few web cites you can go for advice:<br /> A.)<br /> B.)<br /> C.)...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I do miss the old books' page one disclaimer boxes dearly...<br /> <br /> Also, the trend of softening things up, as you put it, is why I'm starting to get sick about the whole &quot;it's just a game for having fun with your friends&quot; argument. I just don't like this whole thing, because &quot;fun&quot; implies something cozy, something where everybody is laughing and enjoying themselves with beer and pretzels and so, it implies that by nature, it should exclude anything anyone at the table (or even the potential readers of a book!) could be uncomfortable with.<br /> <br /> Fun could be a goal, yes, and honestly, most of the time it is the goal of playing rpgs, but it isn't always, particularly in a horror game, just as feeling good and having &quot;fun&quot; isn't always the goal in watching a movie, or reading a book, or going to see an art galery. Yes, you should get something worthwhile back, at the end, because otherwise why doing it in your free time, but it's not always &quot;having fun&quot;. Or, maybe I just misread every DM/ST advice section in every WoD and other horror-themed rpg book in the last 15 years. And I'm not saying anyone should intentionaly traumatize fellow players, because that's not cool, at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would even suggest a game setting neutral book, perhaps a free pdf or something that could discuss this for each game. Something like the April Fools Day releases, (size-wise, not because it is a joke), or Conversion Guides. That would allow for a lot more general discussion and have less need to watch page count, but would also not be an issue with taking up page space in the Wraith book itself, (which to be blunt, has already had too little setting and advice for the game on past editions).<br /> <br /> Something to consider, the ST Vault is a thing, and if you really want this tyoe of thing, or especially if you want, it seems change the meaning of X Cards, why not simply make it yourself and put it up on the Vault? </div> </div> </div>I could get behind that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 10-30-2017, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T10:03:46-07:00","id":1154155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1153930#post1153930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far, this has all been gloriously abstract and philosophical, but, as I said to my high school calculus teacher, &quot;What's it good for?&quot;<br /> <br /> - Have any of the participants played or, even better, run Wraith games? Alternatively, other White Wolf games that deal with similar or equivalent issues? (Like Telgar's example from a Vampire game... Hi Telgar!)<br /> - Did they address these issues either as part of the game set-up, with the players and/or in game when things were on or above the table?<br /> - Did the group go into the game thinking that what they were doing was wrestling with dark issues as ersatz psychotherapy or that they were going to play a game with a group of friends for fun and either not think to address these issues or think about all this or think about it and not deal with it in any structured way?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that all this heady talk isn't as useful or even more useful than a sidebar or a block of text, but, practically, how does this go down in games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, no one got heavily triggered at any table I was playing, ot STing, ever. Not in private games, not at events. I'm not saying it's a non-issue, certainly, there are people out there who have serious traumas and connected triggers, that could came up durng gaming and cause really serious distress to them, but it's just a very-very tiny minority, I believe. Honestly, I think forums like this have a tendency to accumulate such persons, but in real life it's just not a frequent occurence. Yes, people got uncomfortable, even angry at tables sometimes, it got talked out between adults, life went on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 10-30-2017, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T16:56:38-07:00","id":1154253,"title":"","content":"So, I've been lurking on this thread for a bit (disclaimer: I don't okay WoD anymore (Chronicles instead) and have never played Wraith) but I wanted to share an example that I think helps with the whole 'Yeah but it is a mature game, you should know that going in'.<br /> <br /> Spoilered since it is a specific example of death.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> My wife can handle all kinds of horrific stuff, she is not shy about watching lots of horror movies. But you know what turns her into a quivering mass of tears and emotions: old ladies with cancer. Hey, not gore, not rape. People who are still alive but suffering from a disease.<br /> <br /> Why you might ask?<br /> <br /> Because she came home from work one night to find her mother dead on the floor from the cancer she had recently been diagnosed with. She had to sit in her house waiting for the police and paramedics to arrive alone with her mothers corpse because her father had died a couple years previous.<br /> <br /> Of course I know this, and any game with close friends would know this. But should she be in a game at a convention it's not exactly a thing you normally warn people about now is it. It isn't really even a 'dark theme', its just a personal trauma that she has.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T08:46:37-07:00","id":1154391,"title":"","content":"My experiences with player discomfort have more to do with mechanics and storytelling issues than with actual subject matter. I learned some very valuable lessons about STing early on by badly handling player agency in a Mage game. Basic railroading stuff, then doubling down when they rebelled. For most of my players that only killed the fun of the session (which was already enough to show I'd really screwed up), but one of them got really agitated over the loss of control. I'm not sure that agitation had anything to do with their experiences in real life, nor would I share that information if I did, but it did make me rethink what is actually being said in games.<br /> <br /> That's part of why I keep taking a hard look at Shadowguiding. Here you have this thing which is a real part of your character that gives voice to terrible thoughts of worthlessness and spite that are also real parts of your character. Hell it's a real part of your character that actively tries to push them towards ending it all. Google 'Depression lies' and you'll quickly see just one of the ways that this system can remind people of their real life experiences with mental illness.<br /> <br /> And the Shadow is in the hands of another player...<br /> <br /> Which is a feature not a bug. Seriously, the Shadow is one of the best damn parts of this game and a big part of why Wraith has the following it does. The similarity to mental illness and loss of control is not a reason to avoid the issue, lots of people roleplay to work through things in their lives. But good communication is an absolute necessity so that Shadowguides know just what the main player is interested in exploring (and not exploring), and sometimes quick course corrections are necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T19:26:35-07:00","id":1154578,"title":"","content":"I'd like to quote myself for a moment:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm actually fully expecting to see some talk about safety mechanisms in V5, considering the developer team and how important the whole concept is in Nordic LARP and how central and prominent it was in their big LARPs. </div> </div> </div>aaaaand, I'm just listening the interview with Tobias and Martin on Darker Days Radio and Martin just mentioned the x-card and that they'd explicitly tackle these topics in the new edition.<br /> <br /> I should buy a lottery ticket.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T16:38:20-08:00","id":1157150,"title":"","content":"So. Don't know if anyone is a Werewolf player here, but I'd just want to notify that the Book of the Wyrm 20th edition has the following lines in the introduction:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Whether you\u2019re a player or a Storyteller, talk to everyone you\u2019re playing with and ask them one simple question: Is there any subject you\u2019re not comfortable with the game touching on? If anyone says yes, listen to them. Don\u2019t ask for an explanation \u2014 some people will back down if you insist they justify their discomfort, playing along while the story you\u2019re telling makes them feel like shit. Just skip right past that element.<br /> Don\u2019t put it in the game. Likewise, everyone should know that they can say when something that comes up in the game makes them uncomfortable, and you\u2019ll cut that element out. Again, don\u2019t ask questions. Whatever it is, it\u2019s not worth including. </i> </div> </div> </div>And, then again, I believe that you really don't need anything more than this about the personal trauma part. If anything, I hope that Wraith 20 includes some quick reference and hint to set a proper creative agenda with your players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1154578#post1154578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">aaaaand, I'm just listening the interview with Tobias and Martin on Darker Days Radio and Martin just mentioned the x-card and that they'd explicitly tackle these topics in the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just one more reason to never play LARP!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 11-08-2017, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T10:02:07-08:00","id":1157307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1157150#post1157150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just one more reason to never play LARP!</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you please elaborate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T19:59:58-08:00","id":1157425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1157307#post1157307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you please elaborate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the reasons of my disliking of LARPs are IT here. But I'm quite sure that seeing a &quot;no&quot; cards during a LARP would be either a devastating turn off or a reason to complain with the storytellers before leaving the game, so it's just an extra reason for me to avoid them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 11-09-2017, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T09:10:44-08:00","id":1157562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1157425#post1157425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the reasons of my disliking of LARPs are IT here. But I'm quite sure that seeing a &quot;no&quot; cards during a LARP would be either a devastating turn off or a reason to complain with the storytellers before leaving the game, so it's just an extra reason for me to avoid them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the confusion is because the comment you were responding to was talking about the new edition of the tabletop games. Not the LARP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T09:35:24-08:00","id":1157573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1157562#post1157562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the confusion is because the comment you were responding to was talking about the new edition of the tabletop games. Not the LARP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aah, since he quoted the LARP part I thought he was referring to that. Well, it's going to be optional so I see no real issue, but I'm still going to rage at someone if I see red cards when I'm playing at a convention. =p<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 11-10-2017, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T14:14:09-08:00","id":1157635,"title":"","content":"After reading through this thread, I just need to say this; If your RP group in a WoD game, especially in a game like Wraith, isn't a safe place you need to rethink things.<br /> <br /> Wraith basically forces players to question and think a lot about living and death and beliefs. If you cannot trust the group you are with to respect your emotions and responses, or things you want to explore with your character it could get pretty hard emotionally. Because a lot of these things and emotions are pretty raw.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T15:18:31-08:00","id":1157645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1157573#post1157573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aah, since he quoted the LARP part I thought he was referring to that. Well, it's going to be optional so I see no real issue, but I'm still going to rage at someone if I see red cards when I'm playing at a convention. =p</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that they're certainly aware of the concept, since it is very prominent in the Nordic-type LARPs some of them is very experienced in and which served as the &quot;system&quot; for their big WoD LARP events so far. For example, consent-based conflict resolution and scaleable immersion was very talked about and important at Convention of Thorns. So I thought things like that, or the X-card would certainly be in V5, to some extent, based on that and yup, Martin said so in the interview.<br /> <br /> Oh, how outrageously edgelord they are....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T17:30:01-08:00","id":1157662,"title":"","content":"Eh, stuff like the X-card, pre-game briefings and signed contracts to play is very, very necessary in Nordic LARP especially considering the very dark material that is used, blurring of IC and OOC consent and the insane depth of character immersion that is sought after in some Nordic LARP styles and cultures. In most LARPs around the world which at least in the UK, US and Oz tend to be much, much lighter and include tons of OOC interaction in-game time, not so much.....but as they are coming from Nordic LARP where its pretty damn essential to avoid trauma, alienation and attention from the authorities they would be focused that way.<br /> <br /> As for edgelord......well, a number of accounts do tend towards Swedracula not being quite so on top of things regarding consent in the past, hopefully he's learned from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 11-10-2017, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T17:40:43-08:00","id":1157663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1157573#post1157573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aah, since he quoted the LARP part I thought he was referring to that. Well, it's going to be optional so I see no real issue, but I'm still going to rage at someone if I see red cards when I'm playing at a convention. =p</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty sure convention games ( at any decently run convention) would have to have all of their policies mentioned and documented on sign up, so you'd know about consent policies before you got involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T17:49:27-08:00","id":1157665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1157663#post1157663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure convention games ( at any decently run convention) would have to have all of their policies mentioned and documented on sign up, so you'd know about consent policies before you got involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong, my issue is not that people could feel sick or anything. My issue is when a person raises a card to ask to drop the current argument from the scene, if he raises a card and then goes away until it's done I'm fine - even if the ST could need to find a workaround.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T00:14:33-08:00","id":1157708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1157645#post1157645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">consent-based conflict resolution and scaleable immersion</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, talk about an unfortunate choice of labels. I realise that there's some explanation after which it'll be confirmed that first impressions are deceiving, but still, the first impressions from just seeing the labels are terrible: one sounds like an &quot;Five successes I shot you! - No you did not! - Hrmph, okay.&quot; kind of resolution-overriding (and not necessarily just for physical conflicts), the other sounds like a thing that includes 'break immersion' as one of the things it directly does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T11:56:46-08:00","id":1157800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1157662#post1157662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, stuff like the X-card, pre-game briefings and signed contracts to play is very, very necessary in Nordic LARP especially considering the very dark material that is used, blurring of IC and OOC consent and the insane depth of character immersion that is sought after in some Nordic LARP styles and cultures. In most LARPs around the world which at least in the UK, US and Oz tend to be much, much lighter and include tons of OOC interaction in-game time, not so much.....but as they are coming from Nordic LARP where its pretty damn essential to avoid trauma, alienation and attention from the authorities they would be focused that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Yes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for edgelord......well, a number of accounts do tend towards Swedracula not being quite so on top of things regarding consent in the past, hopefully he's learned from that. </div> </div> </div>I know about <i>one </i>case, the infamous &quot;locked a claustrophobic player into a cabinet (or something)&quot;, which I literally don't have any context for, so I'll reserve judgment. What I see is that they're taking this stuff very seriously and I don't think Martin could became the kind of &quot;big name&quot; in Nordic LARP if he wouldn't have done as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 11-11-2017, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T12:24:23-08:00","id":1157804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1157708#post1157708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, talk about an unfortunate choice of labels. I realise that there's some explanation after which it'll be confirmed that first impressions are deceiving, but still, the first impressions from just seeing the labels are terrible: one sounds like an &quot;Five successes I shot you! - No you did not! - Hrmph, okay.&quot; kind of resolution-overriding (and not necessarily just for physical conflicts), the other sounds like a thing that includes 'break immersion' as one of the things it directly does.</div> </div> </div> </div>They gave workshops prior and it was talked about. What I discerned from what I read, these kind of games are very, <i>very</i> rules light to the point that I'd risk to say they didn't have rules in the common tabletop and traditional LARP sense, but more like governing guideances (except for the mentioned stuff - those are quite particular). Mind, the goal is also entirely different as in creating the most satisfying story for the participants with the highest level of immersion and &quot;bleed&quot; as possible. Okay, those are somewhat the same goals as in traditional rpgs, but only at the surface. Nordic LARPs don't tend to do long-term campaigns and objective conflict-resolution isn't really a goal. Physical combat at CoT, for example, was essentially not governed by rules, but the two player negotiating the details and outcome and then acting out it to the extent both were comfortable with.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the whole thing is much more akin to improvisational theater than rpgs to me and I agree with you, it's not the kind of gaming and immersion I'm mostly interested in (and I'd agree too, the things you mentioned might actually break immersion for me, rather than not), but hey, a lot of people seems to like it and these games clearly could be appealing for non-traditional rpg-player type individuals (which, I'd say is a WoD tradition) and they can bring out high levels of immersion and involvement from the participants, so...<br /> <br /> Yeah, not really my cup of tea, but to be honest, it'd be fun to try it out, now and then and the quality WW is doing is convincing. The locale and customs of CoT and Enlightment in Blood, the open-city nature of Berlin, those are good stuff, to be sure. I also think that it <i>is </i>a more outside-audience and media friendly type of gaming than the traditional style, partly because of those things and the emphasis on acting, physicality and high emotions rather than rules-governed play. I'd say that it puts pretty little emphasis on the&quot;game&quot; aspect of rpgs and focuses on the roleplaying, so as I said, it's more like improv-acting to me, but I see how it could be fun for a pretty large audience.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: I haven't attended any of the games and I never played a Nordic LARP and overall I have very little LARP experience. It's totally possible that I got things wrong, but that is what i discerned from reports and some reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 11-11-2017, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T14:43:03-08:00","id":1157817,"title":"","content":"Sorry to be part of the thread delay, but my problem with the whole consent-based resolution thing is that, as far as I am concerned, rules and mechanical resolutions exists (and exists in LARPs especially) when an agreement either cannot be reached, or an impartial arbiter (the random chance on dice rolls) needs to be invoked. If two players and their characters are in a proper conflict, then it should be obvious that at least sometimes, no agreement can be reached, because well, d'uh, its called conflict for a reason.<br /> <br /> Even improv acting tends to have some guidelines apart from character descriptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T15:35:25-08:00","id":1157822,"title":"","content":"Mind, I don't read the rules from any of the games, just some reviews and some stuff about Nordic LARP in general. They might had a bit more concrete guidelines and basic rules, but I think they were not prominent.<br /> <br /> What I see is that this type of LARP basically almost entirely lacks the competitive aspect. Also, as I wrote, Nordic LARP is mostly about high-profile one-shots, with, at least partially pre-generated characters. The goal is just weaving an emotionally fulfilling story, in conjunction with your fellow players and immersing yourself into the situation (which is helped by the high-end locales, props, etc.). You just don't really pursue personal character goals, at the other players' expense, on your own. There is no &quot;surprise assasinations&quot; as such and things like that.<br /> <br /> That's why I'm saying it's pretty far from how I define rpgs, but I'm not saying it's not a hell of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T14:25:54-08:00","id":1159185,"title":"","content":"Sounds more like an elaborate dinner party than a game, but that isn't necessarily bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T17:24:00-08:00","id":1159264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1159185#post1159185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds more like an elaborate dinner party than a game, but that isn't necessarily bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, kinda, as I see it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Again, I didn't attend a game like that so far, but plainly, it's more &quot;collaborative storytelling with awesome props&quot; than &quot;role-playing-<i>game</i>&quot; to me but yeah, that's totally not a bad thing. It's just something different and preferences vary.<br /> <br /> I think it's somewhat like traditional LARP games, like MET are like traditional rpgs and Nordic LARP is more like the farther end of narrative tabletop rpgs. Close enough general concept (playing characters etc.), but totally different styles and focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 11-15-2017, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T14:55:32-08:00","id":1161293,"title":"","content":"The main reason I'm not a fan of modern RPG safety techniques is that they take up space in the rulebook that could be spent on other things.<br /> <br /> I could list others, but the bottom line is that my group never has used them, never will use them, and pretty much any other content would see more mileage at our (virtual) table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T17:43:51-08:00","id":1161352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1147923-modern-rpg-safety-and-wraith20?p=1161293#post1161293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main reason I'm not a fan of modern RPG safety techniques is that they take up space in the rulebook that could be spent on other things.<br /> <br /> I could list others, but the bottom line is that my group never has used them, never will use them, and pretty much any other content would see more mileage at our (virtual) table.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I'm saying putting them in the corebooks is okay, if we contain it to the very basics, but elaborating the thing, I believe specified products are better for that for individuals and groups who'd like to use them. In a Vampire corebook, for example, I'd want it to concrete on how to storytell the Vampire specific stuff well and horror, morality, etc. Safety is/could be a part of that, so put in the basics about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}